{"request_uuid": "a5a0a341-67dd-4fe9-88b6-c2c5702db363", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T09:02:31.957008+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "implementation", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "message_start", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20ccadf0a7e73a6f30a18", "toolName": "edit", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /workspace/loan-payments/adr/plan_20261124-084455.md."}], "details": {"diff": "     ...\n  34 \n  35 ## Implementation Checklist\n  36 Legend: `- [ ]` not started \u00b7 `- [*]` in progress \u00b7 `- [x]` done/passing \u00b7 `- [~]` blocked.\n  37 \n- 38 - [*] 1. Inspect the catalog consumer-loan test data for `Personal_Loan` and `Loan_Payment` to confirm the payload shapes and the edge cases the acceptance criteria rely on (`PL-115`, `PL-011`, the auto-loan rows). [deps: none] \u2192 skill: /data-observation\n+ 38 - [x] 1. Inspect the catalog consumer-loan test data for `Personal_Loan` and `Loan_Payment` to confirm the payload shapes and the edge cases the acceptance criteria rely on (`PL-115`, `PL-011`, the auto-loan rows). [deps: none] \u2192 skill: /data-observation\n  39 - [ ] 2. Scaffold the project next to `lending/` with a main script, an API folder, a snapshots folder, and a README. [deps: none] \u2192 skill: /init-sqrl\n  40 - [ ] 3. Write the `loan-payments-shared-package.json` base plus the `test` and `prod` overlays, declaring the catalog under `script.include`, the Flink/Postgres/Vert.x engine set, the versioned API, and the test runner (FR-1). [deps: 2] \u2192 skill: /configure-sqrl\n  41 - [ ] 4. Define the custom GraphQL schema and operations for the three lookups, keeping the exact table/type names and leaving `customer_id` out of the caller-visible arguments (FR-9, FR-10, FR-11; see `### API surface`). [deps: 2] \u2192 skill: /from-api, /design-api\n  42 - [ ] 5. Configure the Vert.x auth provider in the `test` and `prod` overlays so the claim-reading functions compile (FR-12, FR-13). [deps: 3] \u2192 skill: /configure-sqrl\n     ...", "patch": "--- /workspace/loan-payments/adr/plan_20261124-084455.md\n+++ /workspace/loan-payments/adr/plan_20261124-084455.md\n@@ -34,9 +34,9 @@\n \n ## Implementation Checklist\n Legend: `- [ ]` not started \u00b7 `- [*]` in progress \u00b7 `- [x]` done/passing \u00b7 `- [~]` blocked.\n \n-- [*] 1. Inspect the catalog consumer-loan test data for `Personal_Loan` and `Loan_Payment` to confirm the payload shapes and the edge cases the acceptance criteria rely on (`PL-115`, `PL-011`, the auto-loan rows). [deps: none] \u2192 skill: /data-observation\n+- [x] 1. Inspect the catalog consumer-loan test data for `Personal_Loan` and `Loan_Payment` to confirm the payload shapes and the edge cases the acceptance criteria rely on (`PL-115`, `PL-011`, the auto-loan rows). [deps: none] \u2192 skill: /data-observation\n - [ ] 2. Scaffold the project next to `lending/` with a main script, an API folder, a snapshots folder, and a README. [deps: none] \u2192 skill: /init-sqrl\n - [ ] 3. Write the `loan-payments-shared-package.json` base plus the `test` and `prod` overlays, declaring the catalog under `script.include`, the Flink/Postgres/Vert.x engine set, the versioned API, and the test runner (FR-1). [deps: 2] \u2192 skill: /configure-sqrl\n - [ ] 4. Define the custom GraphQL schema and operations for the three lookups, keeping the exact table/type names and leaving `customer_id` out of the caller-visible arguments (FR-9, FR-10, FR-11; see `### API surface`). [deps: 2] \u2192 skill: /from-api, /design-api\n - [ ] 5. Configure the Vert.x auth provider in the `test` and `prod` overlays so the claim-reading functions compile (FR-12, FR-13). [deps: 3] \u2192 skill: /configure-sqrl\n", "firstChangedLine": 38}, "isError": false, "durationMs": 5, "timestamp": 1795510951956}}
{"request_uuid": "a5a0a341-67dd-4fe9-88b6-c2c5702db363", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T09:02:31.957457+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "implementation", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "message_start", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20ccadf8e79d2bb5f9c09", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "---\nname: init-sqrl\ndescription: Use when starting a new DataSQRL project or initializing an empty pipeline. Use for greenfield implementations, project scaffolding, or setting up the folder structure.\nmodes: [planning, implementation, setup, question]\n---\n\nFollow these steps to initialize a DataSQRL project:\n1. When an available examples directory contains a useful starting point, review its `README.md` and relevant projects. Treat its contents as optional reference material, not required templates.\n2. Adapt relevant example files into the working directory only when they fit the task. Don't overwrite existing files. If no example fits, scaffold the project with `/opt/agent/cmd.sh init <type> <name>` instead (it creates the `<name>/` folder; see `CLI_REFERENCE.md`). Pick the type by the pipeline's output:\n   * `api`: data served through a GraphQL API (Flink, PostgreSQL, Kafka, Vert.x). The production source `connectors/sources-prod.sqrl` is an internal Kafka table (`/*+ engine(kafka) */`), exposed as a mutation.\n   * `stream`: results written to Kafka topics (Flink, Kafka). The production source is an internal Kafka table, and the script exports its result with `EXPORT HelloWorld TO log.HelloWorld;`. Without an API, only exported tables are written anywhere: export each result the user needs, and the script must have at least one `EXPORT` to compile.\n   * `dataset`: results written to Iceberg and queried through DuckDB (Flink, Iceberg, DuckDB). The production source is an existing Iceberg table (`'connector' = 'iceberg'`): set its catalog options (`catalog-type`, `catalog-name`, `warehouse`, `catalog-table`) to the user's lakehouse.\n   * The test package of every type reads the sample data in `connectors/test-data/` and compiles and tests out of the box. Replace the `Messages` sources and the sample data with the real sources (step 4).\n3. Review provided source/sink table definitions in sub-folders to identify the sqrl files that define the sources and sinks required for the implementation. If the requirements reference a provided data catalog, include that catalog and delete copied connectors unless the requirements specifically ask to create additional sources/sinks outside the catalog.\n4. Update copied files to match user requirements by:\n   * **ALWAYS** invoke the relevant skill before updating or implementing anything\n   * Use user-provided source/sink definitions from sub-folders or an included data catalog if they exist (include/import them, reusing what exists), otherwise update the template connectors. Invoke the `/manage-connector` skill (Connector Organization) before writing or editing any source/sink definition.\n   * Updating the SQRL files to use those sources & sinks and adjust implementation by matching the code to the updated table schemas and removing features that are not required. Invoke the `/implement-sqrl` skill before writing or significantly modifying any SQRL logic during this step.\n   * When renaming the main `.sqrl` script, update `script.main` key in the (sub-)project's base config so every package.json reference matches the actual filename before the first compile. When creating or updating any configuration, invoke `/configure-sqrl` skill.\n   * Update the project configuration if necessary.\n   * Update the GraphQL API definition and defined operations to match the new schema.\n   * Create or update the configuration files: a `*-shared-package.json` base plus `*-<env>-package.json` thin per-environment overlays. Invoke the `/configure-sqrl` skill (Base Config and Environment Overlays).\n   * Add `/*+test */` annotated SQL test queries at the end of the main SQRL script(s) for each exposed table. These test queries should SELECT from the table with a WHERE filter on a known test data value and produce deterministic results. Invoke the `/test-sqrl` skill (Writing Tests) for the test and test-data rules, then delete the template's existing snapshots and run the tests to generate fresh ones (Running Tests, Snapshot Lifecycle).\n   * Create or update the test runner script `run-tests.sh` which is the entry point for the project's tests. Invoke the `/test-sqrl` skill for details.\n   * Update `README.md` with user requirements and project description. Add a list of features that are required by the user but not part of the template and need to be implemented\n"}], "isError": false, "durationMs": 2, "timestamp": 1795510951957}}
{"request_uuid": "a5a0a341-67dd-4fe9-88b6-c2c5702db363", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T09:02:31.957929+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "implementation", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "turn_end", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "Data confirms requirements. Note: the test data has no duplicate loan/payment versions? Let me check whether source_updated_at duplicates exist, e.g. multiple versions. The requirements say CDC stream several versions. Let me check distinct loan_id counts = 170 = total loans, so no duplicate versions in personal_loan. Payments distinct payment_id=1942 = total. So no duplicates in test data. Fine.\n\nAlso note PL-115 applied sum = 635360 and returned is 57760. So total_paid_cents for PL-115 = 635360.\n\nNow, step 1 is done. Let me mark it [x].\n\nWait, the plan says \"the acceptance criteria rely on (PL-115, PL-011, the auto-loan rows)\". Confirmed. Let me mark complete and move to step 2.\n\nStep 2: Scaffold the project with init-sqrl. Let me read the init-sqrl skill. Actually the project directory already has adr/ AGENTS.md .datasqrl. There's no .sqrl or package.json. Let me check what init-sqrl requires.\n\nLet me read the init-sqrl, implement-sqrl, configure-sqrl, design-api, from-api, test-sqrl, monitor-pipeline, write-documentation skills. I'll read them as I go. Start with init-sqrl.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20ccadf0a7e73a6f30a18", "name": "edit", "arguments": {"edits": [{"newText": "- [x] 1. Inspect the catalog consumer-loan test data", "oldText": "- [*] 1. Inspect the catalog consumer-loan test data"}], "path": "/workspace/loan-payments/adr/plan_20261124-084455.md"}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20ccadf8e79d2bb5f9c09", "name": "read", "arguments": {"path": "/opt/agent/skills/init-sqrl/SKILL.md"}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "together", "model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.