{"request_uuid": "a5a0a341-67dd-4fe9-88b6-c2c5702db363", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T09:03:12.498558+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "implementation", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "tool_execution_update", "toolCallId": "call_01a20ccb7dad7ab18a3f0510", "toolName": "bash", "args": {"command": "sed -n '1,200p' /opt/datasqrl-examples/feature_store/run-tests.sh | grep -n \"ENVS\\|SUBPROJECTS\\|suite\\|table_test\\|prod\" "}, "partialResult": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "2:# This project's suites \u2014 one command, deterministic exit code.\n8:#   <sub-project>       zero or more names, in any order, selecting which suites run.\n20:#                       line per suite \u2014 exactly the arguments a real run would use\n23:#   ./run-tests.sh                                     test every suite, env test\n25:#   ./run-tests.sh --compile --env local               compile every suite as local\n26:#   ./run-tests.sh --compile --env prod fraud_store    compile just that one, as prod\n36:#   Three blocks below are marked \"EDIT FOR YOUR PROJECT\": the ENVS/SUBPROJECTS declarations,\n37:#   the `suite` table, and the optional setup/teardown hooks. Everything else is boilerplate \u2014\n40:#   The `suite` table is the ONE place a project's config layering is written down: for each\n81:  # different CLI can legitimately produce different output and fail tests that are fine.\n89:# fails loudly instead of matching nothing, running zero suites and still exiting 0.\n90:ENVS=\"test local prod\"\n91:SUBPROJECTS=\"fraud_store fraud_training\"\n105:    --list-envs) echo \"$ENVS\"; exit 0 ;;\n106:    --list-subprojects) echo \"$SUBPROJECTS\"; exit 0 ;;\n112:case \" $ENVS \" in\n114:  *) echo \"unknown env '$ENV' \u2014 this project declares: $ENVS\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n118:  case \" $SUBPROJECTS \" in\n120:    *) echo \"unknown sub-project '$s' \u2014 this project ships: $SUBPROJECTS\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n130:# Each suite writes its own build folder (the -b flag in the driver loop below), so one suite's\n136:  # Every named config must exist. A missing one means the suite line and this environment\n170:# Anything the suites need first \u2014 generating or downloading test data too large for git,\n175:# \u2500\u2500 EDIT FOR YOUR PROJECT: the suite table \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n178:# filenames out literally; any names work. Cover every pair of SUBPROJECTS x ENVS that this\n184:suite() {\n188:    fraud_store/prod)    echo \"fraud_store-shared-package.json fraud_store-prod-package.json\" ;;\n199:for sub in $SUBPROJECTS; do\n"}], "details": {}}}
