{"request_uuid": "a5a0a341-67dd-4fe9-88b6-c2c5702db363", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T09:03:12.499369+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "implementation", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "turn_end", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "The test-sqrl skill confirms: for custom schema exception, name the API test package `<(sub-)project>-api-test-package.json` and table test package `<(sub-)project>-table-test-package.json`. So plan step 10's \"separate inferred-schema table-test package\" = `loan-payments-table-test-package.json`. And step 11's \"custom-schema test package\" = `loan-payments-api-test-package.json`. Good. But plan step 3 said \"the test runner\" and named `loan-payments-test-package.json`. Hmm. The issue is `loan-payments-api-test-package.json` vs `loan-payments-test-package.json`. The skill says name it `<(sub-)project>-test-package.json`, or `<(sub-)project>-api-test-package.json` when the (sub-)project also requires separate table tests. Since we require separate table tests, use `loan-payments-api-test-package.json`. I'll adjust the plan step later to reflect the skill (skill form takes precedence).\n\nSub-projects in run-tests.sh: The skill's exception says: rename `<(sub-)project>-test-package.json` to `<(sub-)project>-api-test-package.json`. Then create `<(sub-)project>-table-test-package.json`. In run-tests.sh, add `<(sub-)project>_table_test` to SUBPROJECTS, and add suite lines:\n- `<(sub-)project>/test) echo \"<shared> <api-test>\" ;;`\n- `<(sub-)project>_table_test/test) echo \"<shared> <table-test>\" ;;`\n\nSo SUBPROJECTS = \"loan-payments loan-payments_table_test\". The main sub-project name is `loan-payments`. The table test sub-project is `loan-payments_table_test`. But `-b <sub-project>` build folder: `build/loan-payments` and `build/loan-payments_table_test`. Good.\n\nNow, the README and plan use `loan-payments-test-package.json`. I'll follow the skill: `loan-payments-api-test-package.json` and `loan-payments-table-test-package.json`. I'll update the plan steps.\n\nWait, but the plan step 3 explicitly names `loan-payments-shared-package.json` base plus the `test` and `prod` overlays. I'll create `loan-payments-shared-package.json`, `loan-payments-prod-package.json`, `loan-payments-api-test-package.json`, `loan-payments-table-test-package.json`. Is there a `loan-payments-test-package.json`? The skill says the API test package can be named `-test-package.json` when no separate table tests. Since we have separate, use `-api-test-package.json`. But the configure-sqrl skill says \"Every independently compiled or tested project and sub-project MUST have a named package file for each environment it uses: `<project>-<env>-package.json`\". Hmm, `api-test` isn't an environment per se. But test-sqrl dictates it. I'll go with the test-sqrl form since it's more specific.\n\nNow, \"Prod compile\" also needed? Step 3 says test and prod overlays. run-tests.sh ENVS = \"test prod\". The suite table would have `loan-payments/prod` and `loan-payments/test`, plus `loan-payments_table_test/test`. The `--env` selects configs. But for prod, the API test package isn't used; we use `loan-payments-shared-package.json loan-payments-prod-package.json`. For test, use shared + api-test. But then `--env test` runs two subprojects: `loan-payments` (with api-test config) and `loan-payments_table_test` (with table-test config). \n\nLet me define suite:\n```\nloan-payments/test) echo \"loan-payments-shared-package.json loan-payments-api-test-package.json\" ;;\nloan-payments/prod) echo \"loan-payments-shared-package.json loan-payments-prod-package.json\" ;;\nloan-payments_table_test/test) echo \"loan-payments-shared-package.json loan-payments-table-test-package.json\" ;;\nloan-payments_table_test/prod) return 1 ;;  # no prod for table test\n```\nBut the run-tests driver loops over SUBPROJECTS for the selected ENV. If ENV=prod and SUBPROJECTS includes loan-payments_table_test, it will error \"no prod configs declared\". That's handled with fail=1. But the default `./run-tests.sh` uses ENV=test, so it only runs test. For `--env prod`, it'd fail on table_test. The skill's feature_store example handles a sub-project without prod. Let me check its run-tests.sh.\n\nActually per the template, the driver loops `for sub in $SUBPROJECTS` and calls `suite \"$sub\" \"$ENV\"`; if missing, prints error and fail=1. So running `--env prod` would mark failure for table_test. That's not great. Let me look at feature_store's script to see how it handles.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20ccb7dad7ab18a3f0510", "name": "bash", "arguments": {"command": "sed -n '1,200p' /opt/datasqrl-examples/feature_store/run-tests.sh | grep -n \"ENVS\\|SUBPROJECTS\\|suite\\|table_test\\|prod\" "}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "together", "model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash", "usage": {"input": 6086, "output": 1189, "cacheRead": 111232, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 1106, "totalTokens": 118507, "cost": {"input": 0.0018257999999999998, "output": 0.0014268, "cacheRead": 0.0006673919999999999, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.003919992}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1795510988424, "responseId": "92bc19b858304b3daaf9f22f2a216288-aws_ec1", "rawStopReason": "tool_calls", "durationMs": 4063, "thinkingLevel": "high"}, "toolResults": [{"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20ccb7dad7ab18a3f0510", "toolName": "bash", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "2:# This project's suites \u2014 one command, deterministic exit code.\n8:#   <sub-project>       zero or more names, in any order, selecting which suites run.\n20:#                       line per suite \u2014 exactly the arguments a real run would use\n23:#   ./run-tests.sh                                     test every suite, env test\n25:#   ./run-tests.sh --compile --env local               compile every suite as local\n26:#   