ly, let me reconsider: maybe simpler to put auth in the base config. Then step 5 is just prod override. The skill explicitly says \"Put it in the shared base...\". And plan step 5 says test and prod overlays. Since skill form takes precedence and both are acceptable, I'll put the auth in the base. Then test overlays inherit. Step 5 becomes \"configure auth in base and prod\". That reduces duplication. But I already wrote the base. Let me edit the base to add auth. Hmm, but then the test secret is in the shared base. For prod, override the issuers array. \n\nActually, I'll follow the plan literally: auth in test and prod overlays. That keeps test secret out of base. Let me write test overlays with auth now (it's cleaner to have complete files), and mark step 5 after.\n\nLet me write `loan-payments-api-test-package.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"script\": {\n    \"config\": { \"environment\": \"test\" }\n  },\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"flink\": {\n      \"config\": { \"table.exec.source.idle-timeout\": \"0 s\" }\n    },\n    \"vertx\": {\n      \"config\": {\n        \"auth\": {\n          \"issuers\": [\n            {\n              \"issuer\": \"loan-payments-test-issuer\",\n              \"audiences\": [\"loan-payments-test-audience\"],\n              \"keys\": [{ \"kty\": \"oct\", \"k\": \"ZHVtbXktc3VwZXItc2VjcmV0LWp3dC1zaWduaW5nLXN0cmluZw\" }]\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"test-runner\": {\n    \"use-inferred-schema\": false,\n    \"delay-sec\": -1,\n    \"required-checkpoints\": 1,\n    \"snapshot-folder\": \"snapshots/loan-payments/\",\n    \"test-folder\": \"loan-payments-api/tests/\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWait, `table.exec.source.idle-timeout: \"0 s\"` \u2014 the test-sqrl skill says keep at 0s in test. But the catalog's test connector has `'source.monitor-interval' = '10 min'` and watermarks. For filesystem sources, idleness? The lending test overlay set `\"1 s\"`. Hmm. The skill says keep 0s because the test runner disables idleness. But lending uses 1s. The catalog's ontology-test-package sets 1s. I'll use \"0 s\" per skill. Actually the skill: \"Keep `table.exec.source.idle-timeout` at `\"0 s\"` in the test package, because the test runner disables idleness. If a base package sets it, override it with `\"0 s\"` in the test overlay.\" OK use 0s.\n\nThe table-test package:\n```json\n{\n  \"script\": { \"config\": { \"environment\": \"test\" } },\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"flink\": { \"config\": { \"table.exec.source.idle-timeout\": \"0 s\" } },\n    \"vertx\": { \"config\": { \"auth\": { ... same ... } } }\n  },\n  \"test-runner\": {\n    \"use-inferred-schema\": true,\n    \"delay-sec\": -1,\n    \"required-checkpoints\": 1,\n    \"snapshot-folder\": \"snapshots/loan-payments_table_test/\",\n    \"test-folder\": \"no-graphql-tests/\",\n    \"headers\": { \"Authorization\": \"Bearer <CUST-060>\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nProd:\n```json\n{\n  \"script\": { \"config\": { \"environment\": \"prod\" } },\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"vertx\": {\n      \"config\": {\n        \"auth\": {\n          \"issuers\": [\n            {\n              \"issuer\": \"${AUTH_ISSUER}\",\n              \"audiences\": [\"${AUTH_AUDIENCE}\"],\n              \"keys\": [{ \"kty\": \"oct\", \"k\": \"${JWT_SECRET}\" }]\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWait, prod also needs is_batch config? The include config already sets is_batch false. Good.\n\nProd environment: should we add deployment sizing? Plan assumption \"smallest DataSQRL Cloud deployment size\". Step 3 doesn't require deployment. The optimize-deployment skill triggers on sizing. The plan's budget assumption says smallest. Let me add deployment sizing to prod? The plan step 3 mentions \"the Flink/Postgres/Vert.x engine set\". Not deployment. The task says invoke optimize-deployment when setting deployment sizes. Since budget is \"smallest\", I could add. But to keep scope minimal and avoid invoking optimize-deployment, I'll not set deployment sizes; defaults apply. The plan assumption says default. Actually \"smallest DataSQRL Cloud deployment\" may be default. Let me leave deployment unspecified. Hmm, but prod compile should produce deployment artifacts; defaults are fine.\n\nWait, one concern: prod uses `${JWT_SECRET}` for the `k` value. But `k` must be base64url. The environment variable would need to contain base64url. The plan says \"a key from ${JWT_SECRET}\". OK.\n\nAlso, the `issuer` and `audiences` env vars: `${AUTH_ISSUER}` and `${AUTH_AUDIENCE}`. Fine.\n\nNow, let me write these three overlays. Then step 4 API files."}}
