{"request_uuid": "a5a0a341-67dd-4fe9-88b6-c2c5702db363", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T09:04:10.814880+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "implementation", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "turn_end", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "Now mark steps 3 and 4 complete. Then step 6 implement the script (step 5 auth already done). Let me update the plan.\n\nActually step 5 is configure auth \u2014 I already did in the overlays. I'll mark 5 done too. Step 6 implement script.\n\nLet me write the main script now. I'll invoke implement-sqrl skill (already read). Let me write the full script.\n\nConsiderations:\n- `IMPORT data_catalog...` \u2014 the namespace key is `data_catalog`. The skill says relative import from consumer: `IMPORT data_catalog.lending.cards_consumer_credit.consumer_loans-{{environment}} AS cons_loans;`. Good.\n- But the include root is `../data-catalog`. The `consumer_loans-test.sqrl` does `IMPORT consumer_loans.*;` relative to itself. Good.\n\nLet me write the script.\n\nOne concern: `_LatestPersonalLoan` DISTINCT ordered by `source_updated_at DESC`. The requirement FR-2. Good.\n\nAnother: Deduplicating payments: `DISTINCT cons_loans.Loan_Payment ON payment_id ORDER BY source_updated_at DESC`. Then filter `loan_type='PERSONAL'`. Good.\n\n`LoanPaymentsSource` join with latest loans. The requirement says inner join. Good.\n\nAggregation `_AppliedPaymentAgg`: count of APPLIED, sums. Note `late_fees_paid_cents`: sum of late_fee_cents (nullable). `SUM` ignores nulls. `COALESCE(..., 0)` at the summary.\n\nWait, FR-6 says late_fees_paid_cents is sum of late_fee_cents. It doesn't say only nonzero. SUM handles null. Good.\n\nAlso, `principal_paid_cents` sum of principal_cents (nullable). Good.\n\n`returned_payment_count`: count of RETURNED.\n\nNow `LoanPaymentSummarySource` anchored on `_LatestPersonalLoan` left join both aggregations. Good.\n\n`CustomerLoansSource`: join `_LatestPersonalLoan` to `LoanPaymentSummarySource` on loan_id. Actually `LoanPaymentSummarySource` already anchored on `_LatestPersonalLoan`; joining again is redundant but fine. Could just select from `LoanPaymentSummarySource` and add loan details, but summary source doesn't have loan details. So join.\n\nFunctions with claim `customer_id`.\n\nTable tests.\n\nLet me also add `/*+test(no_rows)*/` tests for data integrity:\n- Auto loan leak: `WHERE loan_id LIKE 'AL-%'` \u2014 actually FR-1/FR-3 says no `AL-` loan ids. Since we filter loan_type='PERSONAL' and join latest loans, AL- shouldn't appear.\n- Duplicate payment: group by payment_id HAVING count>1.\n- Duplicate summary loan: group by loan_id HAVING count>1.\n- Row count test.\n\nLet me write.\n\nActually, I realize the `_LatestPersonalLoan` might be considered a VERSIONED_STATE with primary key loan_id. The left join with aggregates. Fine.\n\nLet me write the script.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Steps 3\u20135 are done. Now step 6\u20138: implement the main SQRL script."}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20ccc584d7ad3ac10e73d", "name": "edit", "arguments": {"edits": [{"newText": "- [x] 3. Write the `loan-payments-shared-package.json` base", "oldText": "- [*] 3. Write the `loan-payments-shared-package.json` base"}, {"newText": "- [x] 4. Define the custom GraphQL schema and operations", "oldText": "- [ ] 4. Define the custom GraphQL schema and operations"}, {"newText": "- [x] 5. Configure the Vert.x auth provider", "oldText": "- [ ] 5. Configure the Vert.x auth provider"}, {"newText": "- [*] 6. Implement the `LoanPayments` table", "oldText": "- [ ] 6. Implement the `LoanPayments` table"}], "path": "/workspace/loan-payments/adr/plan_20261124-084455.md"}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20ccc59557be08668f414", "name": "write", "arguments": {"content": "-- Loan Payments API: personal-loan payment history and per-loan summary for customers.\n--\n-- Sources are the shared data-catalog consumer-loan tables. The pipeline owns no data of its own:\n-- it deduplicates the catalog's CDC streams, keeps only personal-loan payments, enriches them from\n-- their loan record, and exposes three lookups that every filter by the caller's customer_id claim.\n\nIMPORT data_catalog.lending.cards_consumer_credit.consumer_loans-{{environment}} AS cons_loans;\n\n-- FR-2: keep the latest version of each loan and payment (CDC streams, at-least-once).\n_LatestPersonalLoan := DISTINCT cons_loans.Personal_Loan ON loan_id ORDER BY source_updated_at DESC;\n_LatestLoanPayment := DISTINCT cons_loans.Loan_Payment ON payment_id ORDER BY source_updated_at DESC;\n\n-- FR-3: only personal-loan payments. Auto-loan payments are out of scope.\n_LatestPersonalLoanPayment :=\n  SELECT * FROM _LatestLoanPayment WHERE loan_type = 'PERSONAL';\n\n-- FR-4, FR-5: one row per payment in every status, enriched with the customer and purpose of the\n-- loan it belongs to. The inner join also enforces that the loan exists in Personal_Loan.\n/*+no_query */\nLoanPaymentsSource :=\n  SELECT p.payment_id,\n         p.loan_id,\n         l.primary_borrower_customer_id AS customer_id,\n         l.loan_purpose,\n         p.payment_amount_cents,\n         p.principal_cents,\n         p.interest_cents,\n         p.late_fee_cents,\n         p.other_fees_cents,\n         p.payment_type,\n         p.payment_status,\n         p.due_date,\n         p.received_date,\n         p.applied_date,\n         p.payment_method,\n         p.principal_balance_after_cents,\n         p.days_past_due_at_payment,\n         p.confirmation_number,\n         p.return_reason_code\n  FROM _LatestPersonalLoanPayment p\n  JOIN _LatestPersonalLoan l ON p.loan_id = l.loan_id;\n\n-- FR-7: only APPLIED payments contribute to the totals and the last payment date.\n_AppliedPaymentAgg :=\n  SELECT loan_id,\n         COUNT(*) AS applied_payment_count,\n         SUM(payment_amount_cents) AS total_paid_cents,\n         SUM(principal_cents) AS principal_paid_cents,\n         SUM(interest_cents) AS interest_paid_cents,\n         SUM(late_fee_cents) AS late_fees_paid_cents,\n         MAX(applied_date) AS last_payment_date\n  FROM LoanPaymentsSource\n  WHERE payment_status = 'APPLIED'\n  GROUP BY loan_id;\n\n_ReturnedPaymentAgg :=\n  SELECT loan_id, COUNT(*) AS returned_payment_count\n  FROM LoanPaymentsSource\n  WHERE payment_status = 'RETURNED'\n  GROUP BY loan_id;\n\n-- FR-6: one row per personal loan, anchored on the latest loans so a loan without payments still\n-- appears with zero counts and sums and a null last payment date.\n/*+no_query */\nLoanPaymentSummarySource :=\n  SELECT l.loan_id,\n         l.primary_borrower_customer_id AS customer_id,\n         l.loan_purpose,\n         COALESCE(a.applied_payment_count, 0) AS applied_payment_count,\n         COALESCE(r.returned_payment_count, 0) AS returned_payment_count,\n         COALESCE(a.total_paid_cents, 0) AS total_paid_cents,\n         COALESCE(a.principal_paid_cents, 0) AS principal_paid_cents,\n         COALESCE(a.interest_paid_cents, 0) AS interest_paid_cents,\n         COALESCE(a.late_fees_paid_cents, 0) AS late_fees_paid_cents,\n         a.last_payment_date\n  FROM _LatestPersonalLoan l\n  LEFT JOIN _AppliedPaymentAgg a ON l.loan_id = a.loan_id\n  LEFT JOIN _ReturnedPaymentAgg r ON l.loan_id = r.loan_id;\n\n-- FR-11: the signed-in customer's loans with their summary and the loan details the client shows.\n/*+no_query */\nCustomerLoansSource :=\n  SELECT l.loan_id,\n         l.primary_borrower_customer_id AS customer_id,\n         l.loan_purpose,\n         l.loan_status,\n         l.original_amount_cents,\n         l.current_balance_cents,\n         l.monthly_payment_cents,\n         l.next_payment_due_date,\n         s.applied_payment_count,\n         s.returned_payment_count,\n         s.total_paid_cents,\n         s.principal_paid_cents,\n         s.interest_paid_cents,\n         s.late_fees_paid_cents,\n         s.last_payment_date\n  FROM _LatestPersonalLoan l\n  JOIN LoanPaymentSummarySource s ON l.loan_id = s.loan_id;\n\n-- FR-9, FR-12: summary of one loan, filtered by the JWT claim so another customer's loan is invisible.\nLoanPaymentSummary(loan_id STRING NOT NULL, customer_id STRING NOT NULL METADATA FROM 'auth.customer_id') :=\n  SELECT * FROM LoanPaymentSummarySource\n  WHERE loan_id = :loan_id AND customer_id = :customer_id;\n\n-- FR-10, FR-12: payments of one loan, newest due date first, same claim filter.\nLoanPayments(loan_id STRING NOT NULL, customer_id STRING NOT NULL METADATA FROM 'auth.customer_id') :=\n  SELECT * FROM LoanPaymentsSource\n  WHERE loan_id = :loan_id AND customer_id = :customer_id\n  ORDER BY due_date DESC, payment_id;\n\n-- FR-11, FR-12: every personal loan of the signed-in customer, each with its summary.\nCustomerLoans(customer_id STRING NOT NULL METADATA FROM 'auth.customer_id') :=\n  SELECT * FROM CustomerLoansSource\n  WHERE customer_id = :customer_id\n  ORDER BY loan_id;\n\n/* ==== TABLE TESTS (run by loan-payments-table-test-package.json against the inferred schema) ==== */\n\n-- FR-1, FR-3: exactly the 1,010 personal payments remain; no auto-loan payment leaked in.\n/*+test */\nLoanPaymentsCountTest :=\n  SELECT COUNT(*) AS payment_rows, COUNT(DISTINCT loan_id) AS loans_with_payments\n  FROM LoanPaymentsSource;\n\n/*+test(no_rows) */\nAutoLoanLeakTest :=\n  SELECT * FROM LoanPaymentsSource WHERE loan_id LIKE 'AL-%';\n\n-- FR-2: one row per payment_id and one row per loan_id.\n/*+test(no_rows) */\nDuplicateLoanPaymentsTest :=\n  SELECT payment_id, COUNT(*) AS num_rows\n  FROM LoanPaymentsSource GROUP BY payment_id HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;\n\n/*+test(no_rows) */\nDuplicateLoanSummaryTest :=\n  SELECT loan_id, COUNT(*) AS num_rows\n  FROM LoanPaymentSummarySource GROUP BY loan_id HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;\n\n-- FR-6: a loan without payments has zero counts and sums and a null last payment date.\n/*+test */\nZeroPaymentSummaryTest :=\n  SELECT loan_id, applied_payment_count, returned_payment_count, total_paid_cents, last_payment_date\n  FROM LoanPaymentSummarySource WHERE loan_id = 'PL-011';\n", "path": "/workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments.sqrl"}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "together", "model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash", "usage": {"input": 127, "output": 2620, "cacheRead": 144640, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 672, "totalTokens": 147387, "cost": {"input": 3.81e-05, "output": 0.0031439999999999997, "cacheRead": 0.00086784, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.00404994}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1795511044098, "responseId": "50ef7b3a970d4e5f8767a87ed68f8072-aws_ec1", "rawStopReason": "tool_calls", "durationMs": 6708, "thinkingLevel": "high"}, "toolResults": [{"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20ccc584d7ad3ac10e73d", "toolName": "edit", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced 4 block(s) in /workspace/loan-payments/adr/plan_20261124-084455.md."}], "details": {"diff": "     ...\n  36 Legend: `- [ ]` not started \u00b7 `- [*]` in progress \u00b7 `- [x]` done/passing \u00b7 `- [~]` blocked.\n  37 \n  38 - [x] 1. Inspect the catalog consumer-loan test data for `Personal_Loan` and `Loan_Payment` to confirm the payload shapes and the edge cases the acceptance criteria rely on (`PL-115`, `PL-011`, the auto-loan rows). [deps: none] \u2192 skill: /data-observation\n  39 - [x] 2. Scaffold the project next to `lending/` with a main script, an API folder, a snapshots folder, and a README. [deps: none] \u2192 skill: /init-sqrl\n- 40 - [*] 3. Write the `loan-payments-shared-package.json` base plus the `test` and `prod` overlays, declaring the catalog under `script.include`, the Flink/Postgres/Vert.x engine set, the versioned API, and the test runner (FR-1). [deps: 2] \u2192 skill: /configure-sqrl\n- 41 - [ ] 4. Define the custom GraphQL schema and operations for the three lookups, keeping the exact table/type names and leaving `customer_id` out of the caller-visible arguments (FR-9, FR-10, FR-11; see `### API surface`). [deps: 2] \u2192 skill: /from-api, /design-api\n- 42 - [ ] 5. Configure the Vert.x auth provider in the `test` and `prod` overlays so the claim-reading functions compile (FR-12, FR-13). [deps: 3] \u2192 skill: /configure-sqrl\n- 43 - [ ] 6. Implement the `LoanPayments` table: import the catalog consumer-loan scripts, keep the latest version of each loan and payment by `source_updated_at`, retain only `loan_type = 'PERSONAL'` payments, and enrich them from their loan record (FR-1\u2013FR-5, `### Transformations and aggregations` items 1\u20133). [deps: 3] \u2192 skill: /implement-sqrl\n+ 40 - [x] 3. Write the `loan-payments-shared-package.json` base plus the `test` and `prod` overlays, declaring the catalog under `script.include`, the Flink/Postgres/Vert.x engine set, the versioned API, and the test runner (FR-1). [deps: 2] \u2192 skill: /configure-sqrl\n+ 41 - [x] 4. Define the custom GraphQL schema and operations for the three lookups, keeping the exact table/type names and leaving `customer_id` out of the caller-visible arguments (FR-9, FR-10, FR-11; see `### API surface`). [deps: 2] \u2192 skill: /from-api, /design-api\n+ 42 - [x] 5. Configure the Vert.x auth provider in the `test` and `prod` overlays so the claim-reading functions compile (FR-12, FR-13). [deps: 3] \u2192 skill: /configure-sqrl\n+ 43 - [*] 6. Implement the `LoanPayments` table: import the catalog consumer-loan scripts, keep the latest version of each loan and payment by `source_updated_at`, retain only `loan_type = 'PERSONAL'` payments, and enrich them from their loan record (FR-1\u2013FR-5, `### Transformations and aggregations` items 1\u20133). [deps: 3] \u2192 skill: /implement-sqrl\n  44 - [ ] 7. Implement `LoanPaymentSummary` anchored on all latest personal loans and left-joined to the applied-payment aggregates, so only `APPLIED` payments contribute totals and a loan with no payments gets zero counts and a null last payment date (FR-6, FR-7, FR-8). [deps: 6] \u2192 skill: /implement-sqrl\n  45 - [ ] 8. Add the three authorization-filtered lookups \u2014 summary by `loan_id`, payments by `loan_id`, and the signed-in customer's loans with their summaries \u2014 reading the `customer_id` claim (FR-9\u2013FR-12). [deps: 4, 7] \u2192 skill: /implement-sqrl, /design-api\n  46 - [ ] 9. Review the completed pipeline for data-quality and observability gaps and add tables only where a credible failure is unguarded; otherwise record why nothing new is needed (see `## Data Quality & Observability`). [deps: 8] \u2192 skill: /monitor-pipeline\n  47 - [ ] 10. Add a separate inferred-schema table-test package covering the data-integrity criteria: personal-only row count, absence of `AL-` loan ids, and one row per `payment_id` and per `loan_id` (FR-1, FR-2, FR-3). [deps: 9] \u2192 skill: /test-sqrl\n     ...", "patch": "--- /workspace/loan-payments/adr/plan_20261124-084455.md\n+++ /workspace/loan-payments/adr/plan_20261124-084455.md\n@@ -36,12 +36,12 @@\n Legend: `- [ ]` not started \u00b7 `- [*]` in progress \u00b7 `- [x]` done/passing \u00b7 `- [~]` blocked.\n \n - [x] 1. Inspect the catalog consumer-loan test data for `Personal_Loan` and `Loan_Payment` to confirm the payload shapes and the edge cases the acceptance criteria rely on (`PL-115`, `PL-011`, the auto-loan rows). [deps: none] \u2192 skill: /data-observation\n - [x] 2. Scaffold the project next to `lending/` with a main script, an API folder, a snapshots folder, and a README. [deps: none] \u2192 skill: /init-sqrl\n-- [*] 3. Write the `loan-payments-shared-package.json` base plus the `test` and `prod` overlays, declaring the catalog under `script.include`, the Flink/Postgres/Vert.x engine set, the versioned API, and the test runner (FR-1). [deps: 2] \u2192 skill: /configure-sqrl\n-- [ ] 4. Define the custom GraphQL schema and operations for the three lookups, keeping the exact table/type names and leaving `customer_id` out of the caller-visible arguments (FR-9, FR-