{"request_uuid": "a5a0a341-67dd-4fe9-88b6-c2c5702db363", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T09:07:50.492190+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "implementation", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "message_start", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20ccfbba07751b799bc96", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "- [x] 2. Scaffold the project next to `lending/` with a main script, an API folder, a snapshots folder, and a README. [deps: none] \u2192 skill: /init-sqrl\n- [x] 3. Write the `loan-payments-shared-package.json` base plus the `test` and `prod` overlays, declaring the catalog under `script.include`, the Flink/Postgres/Vert.x engine set, the versioned API, and the test runner (FR-1). [deps: 2] \u2192 skill: /configure-sqrl\n- [x] 4. Define the custom GraphQL schema and operations for the three lookups, keeping the exact table/type names and leaving `customer_id` out of the caller-visible arguments (FR-9, FR-10, FR-11; see `### API surface`). [deps: 2] \u2192 skill: /from-api, /design-api\n- [x] 5. Configure the Vert.x auth provider in the `test` and `prod` overlays so the claim-reading functions compile (FR-12, FR-13). [deps: 3] \u2192 skill: /configure-sqrl\n- [x] 6. Implement the `LoanPayments` table: import the catalog consumer-loan scripts, keep the latest version of each loan and payment by `source_updated_at`, retain only `loan_type = 'PERSONAL'` payments, and enrich them from their loan record (FR-1\u2013FR-5, `### Transformations and aggregations` items 1\u20133). [deps: 3] \u2192 skill: /implement-sqrl\n- [x] 7. Implement `LoanPaymentSummary` anchored on all latest personal loans and left-joined to the applied-payment aggregates, so only `APPLIED` payments contribute totals and a loan with no payments gets zero counts and a null last payment date (FR-6, FR-7, FR-8). [deps: 6] \u2192 skill: /implement-sqrl\n- [x] 8. Add the three authorization-filtered lookups \u2014 summary by `loan_id`, payments by `loan_id`, and the signed-in customer's loans with their summaries \u2014 reading the `customer_id` claim (FR-9\u2013FR-12). [deps: 4, 7] \u2192 skill: /implement-sqrl, /design-api\n- [x] 9. Review the completed pipeline for data-quality and observability gaps and add tables only where a credible failure is unguarded; otherwise record why nothing new is needed (see `## Data Quality & Observability`). [deps: 8] \u2192 skill: /monitor-pipeline\n- [x] 10. Add a separate inferred-schema table-test package covering the data-integrity criteria: personal-only row count, absence of `AL-` loan ids, and one row per `payment_id` and per `loan_id` (FR-1, FR-2, FR-3). [deps: 9] \u2192 skill: /test-sqrl\n- [x] 11. Add API tests in the custom-schema test package for the snapshot criteria and JWT cases: the returned payment, a loan with applied late fees, the zero-payment loan, the four-loan customer, a wrong customer, and a missing token (acceptance criteria for FR-5\u2013FR-13). [deps: 9] \u2192 skill: /test-sqrl\n- [x] 12. Create `run-tests.sh` declaring the `test`/`prod` environments and both test suites, then run it and regenerate the snapshots. [deps: 10, 11] \u2192 skill: /test-sqrl\n- [x] 13. Document the project, its sources, its API, the authorization model, and how FR-8 is covered in the README. [deps: 12] \u2192 skill: /write-documentation\n- [~] 14. [cond: tests fail after step 12] Diagnose and fix the failing compile or snapshot. \u2014 skipped: all 13 tests passed on the step-12 run. [deps: 12] \u2192 skill: /troubleshoot-test\n\n## Data Quality & Observability\n- **Build** \u2014 none new. The one credible silent-loss point is the inner join from personal\n  payments to `Personal_Loan`: a `PERSONAL` payment whose loan record never arrives would vanish\n  from `LoanPayments` and undercount its summary. The catalog already guarantees this cannot\n  happen (`LoanPaymentReferencesValidPersonalLoan_Test` in\n  `data-catalog/lending/lending-ontology.sqrl`), so no capture table is warranted. FR-8 is handled\n\n[78 more lines in file. Use offset=59 to continue.]"}], "isError": false, "durationMs": 3, "timestamp": 1795511270491}}
