    \"issuers\": [\n            {\n              \"issuer\": \"${AUTH_ISSUER}\",\n              \"audiences\": [\"${AUTH_AUDIENCE}\"],\n              \"keys\": [{ \"kty\": \"oct\", \"k\": \"${JWT_SECRET}\" }]\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n", "path": "/workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments-prod-package.json"}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "together", "model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash", "usage": {"input": 135, "output": 2574, "cacheRead": 139520, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 1563, "totalTokens": 142229, "cost": {"input": 4.0499999999999995e-05, "output": 0.0030888, "cacheRead": 0.00083712, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.00396642}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1795511033233, "responseId": "06b7fecedd004254a7d52fd19a7c1e56-aws_ec1", "rawStopReason": "tool_calls", "durationMs": 5698, "thinkingLevel": "high"}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20ccc2e727833b9abdb05", "toolName": "write", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully wrote to /workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments-api-test-package.json"}], "isError": false, "durationMs": 4, "timestamp": 1795511038938}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20ccc30147950ad844250", "toolName": "write", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully wrote to /workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments-table-test-package.json"}], "isError": false, "durationMs": 4, "timestamp": 1795511038938}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20ccc32a3799384a46d5c", "toolName": "write", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully wrote to /workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments-prod-package.json"}], "isError": false, "durationMs": 4, "timestamp": 1795511038938}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "Now step 3 done. Step 4: API schema and operations. Let me write the schema.\n\nCustom schema needs scalars Date, Long; maybe DateTime not needed. And the `@api` directive. Let me write.\n\n```graphql\n\"An RFC-3339 compliant date (no time component).\"\nscalar Date\n\n\"A 64-bit signed integer.\"\nscalar Long\n\n\"Per-loan totals and counts over the payments of one personal loan.\"\ntype LoanPaymentSummary {\n  loan_id: String!\n  customer_id: String!\n  loan_purpose: String\n  applied_payment_count: Long!\n  returned_payment_count: Long!\n  total_paid_cents: Long!\n  principal_paid_cents: Long!\n  interest_paid_cents: Long!\n  late_fees_paid_cents: Long!\n  last_payment_date: Date\n}\n\n\"One payment of a personal loan.\"\ntype LoanPayments {\n  payment_id: String!\n  loan_id: String!\n  customer_id: String!\n  loan_purpose: String\n  payment_amount_cents: Long!\n  principal_cents: Long\n  interest_cents: Long\n  late_fee_cents: Long\n  other_fees_cents: Long\n  payment_type: String!\n  payment_status: String!\n  due_date: Date!\n  received_date: Date\n  applied_date: Date\n  payment_method: String\n  principal_balance_after_cents: Long\n  days_past_due_at_payment: Int\n  confirmation_number: String\n  return_reason_code: String\n}\n\n\"One personal loan of the signed-in customer, with its payment summary.\"\ntype CustomerLoans {\n  loan_id: String!\n  customer_id: String!\n  loan_purpose: String\n  loan_status: String!\n  original_amount_cents: Long!\n  current_balance_cents: Long!\n  monthly_payment_cents: Long!\n  next_payment_due_date: Date\n  applied_payment_count: Long!\n  returned_payment_count: Long!\n  total_paid_cents: Long!\n  principal_paid_cents: Long!\n  interest_paid_cents: Long!\n  late_fees_paid_cents: Long!\n  last_payment_date: Date\n}\n\ntype Query {\n  \"Payment summary of one loan owned by the signed-in customer. Returns null when the loan does not exist or belongs to another customer.\"\n  LoanPaymentSummary(loan_id: String!): LoanPaymentSummary\n  \"Payments of one loan owned by the signed-in customer, newest due date first.\"\n  LoanPayments(loan_id: String!, limit: Int = 20, offset: Int = 0): [LoanPayments!]\n  \"All personal loans of the signed-in customer, each with its payment summary.\"\n  CustomerLoans(limit: Int = 20, offset: Int = 0): [CustomerLoans!]\n}\n\nenum _McpMethodType { NONE TOOL }\nenum _RestMethodType { NONE GET POST }\ndirective @api(mcp: _McpMethodType, rest: _RestMethodType, uri: String) on QUERY | MUTATION | FIELD_DEFINITION\n```\n\nWait, `LoanPaymentSummary(loan_id: String!)` returns single object. The function returns at most one row. Good.\n\nNow operations.v1.graphql:\n```graphql\n# Payment summary of one loan for the signed-in customer.\nquery LoanSummaryByLoan($loan_id: String!) @api(mcp: TOOL, rest: GET, uri: \"/loans/{loan_id}/payment-summary\") {\n  LoanPaymentSummary(loan_id: $loan_id) { ... }\n}\n\n# Payments of one loan for the signed-in customer, newest due date first.\nquery LoanPaymentsByLoan($loan_id: String!, $limit: Int = 20, $offset: Int = 0) @api(mcp: TOOL, rest: GET, uri: \"/loans/{loan_id}/payments{?limit,offset}\") {\n  LoanPayments(loan_id: $loan_id, limit: $limit, offset: $offset) { ... }\n}\n\n# All personal loans of the signed-in customer.\nquery MyLoans @api(mcp: TOOL, rest: GET, uri: \"/my-loans\") {\n  CustomerLoans { ... }\n}\n```\n\nHmm `MyLoans` has no arguments and returns a list. Fine. REST GET.\n\nNow, the `CustomerLoans` field has limit/offset defaults. Including limit/offset in the operation as variables isn't required.\n\nLet me write the schema file. Note the `@api` directive definition is already in the schema; operations file uses it.\n\nNow, is the `LoanPaymentSummary(loan_id: String!)` single object allowed by SQRL when the function returns a list? The function returns rows; the schema declares a single object. The design-api says cardinality changes are allowed. Good.\n\nLet me write both files.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Step 3 done. Now step 4: the custom GraphQL schema and operations."}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20ccc42007d019648e5ab", "name": "write", "arguments": {"content": "\"An RFC-3339 compliant date without a time component.\"\nscalar Date\n\n\"A 64-bit signed integer.\"\nscalar Long\n\n\"Per-loan payment counts and totals for one personal loan. Totals and the last payment date cover only APPLIED payments.\"\ntype LoanPaymentSummary {\n  loan_id: String!\n  customer_id: String!\n  loan_purpose: String\n  applied_payment_count: Long!\n  returned_payment_count: Long!\n  total_paid_cents: Long!\n  principal_paid_cents: Long!\n  interest_paid_cents: Long!\n  late_fees_paid_cents: Long!\n  last_payment_date: Date\n}\n\n\"One payment of a personal loan, in every payment status.\"\ntype LoanPayments {\n  payment_id: String!\n  loan_id: String!\n  customer_id: String!\n  loan_purpose: String\n  payment_amount_cents: Long!\n  principal_cents: Long\n  interest_cents: Long\n  late_fee_cents: Long\n  other_fees_cents: Long\n  payment_type: String!\n  payment_status: String!\n  due_date: Date!\n  received_date: Date\n  applied_date: Date\n  payment_method: String\n  principal_balance_after_cents: Long\n  days_past_due_at_payment: Int\n  confirmation_number: String\n  return_reason_code: String\n}\n\n\"One personal loan of the signed-in customer together with its payment summary.\"\ntype CustomerLoans {\n  loan_id: String!\n  customer_id: String!\n  loan_purpose: String\n  loan_status: String!\n  original_amount_cents: Long!\n  current_balance_cents: Long!\n  monthly_payment_cents: Long!\n  next_payment_due_date: Date\n  applied_payment_count: Long!\n  returned_payment_count: Long!\n  total_paid_cents: Long!\n  principal_paid_cents: Long!\n  interest_paid_cents: Long!\n  late_fees_paid_cents: Long!\n  last_payment_date: Date\n}\n\ntype Query {\n  \"Payment summary of one loan owned by the signed-in customer. Returns null when the loan does not exist or belongs to another customer.\"\n  LoanPaymentSummary(loan_id: String!): LoanPaymentSummary\n  \"Payments of one loan owned by the signed-in customer, newest due date first, paged with limit and offset.\"\n  LoanPayments(loan_id: String!, limit: Int = 20, offset: Int = 0): [LoanPayments!]\n  \"Every personal loan of the signed-in customer, each with its payment summary.\"\n  CustomerLoans(limit: Int = 20, offset: Int = 0): [CustomerLoans!]\n}\n\nenum _McpMethodType {\n  NONE\n  TOOL\n}\n\nenum _RestMethodType {\n  NONE\n  GET\n  POST\n}\n\ndirective @api(mcp: _McpMethodType, rest: _RestMethodType, uri: String) on QUERY | MUTATION | FIELD_DEFINITION\n", "path": "/workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments-api/schema.v1.graphqls"}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20ccc453f7b628b1894e4", "name": "write", "arguments": {"content": "# Payment summary of one loan owned by the signed-in customer.\n# The customer is taken from the JWT claim customer_id, so a caller cannot ask for another customer.\nquery LoanSummaryByLoan($loan_id: String!) @api(mcp: TOOL, rest: GET, uri: \"/loans/{loan_id}/payment-summary\") {\n  LoanPaymentSummary(loan_id: $loan_id) {\n    loan_id\n    customer_id\n    loan_purpose\n    applied_payment_count\n    returned_payment_count\n    total_paid_cents\n    principal_paid_cents\n    interest_paid_cents\n    late_fees_paid_cents\n    last_payment_date\n  }\n}\n\n# Payments of one loan owned by the signed-in customer, newest due date first.\nquery LoanPaymentsByLoan($loan_id: String!, $limit: Int = 20, $offset: Int = 0) @api(mcp: TOOL, rest: GET, uri: \"/loans/{loan_id}/payments{?limit,offset}\") {\n  LoanPayments(loan_id: $loan_id, limit: $limit, offset: $offset) {\n    payment_id\n    loan_id\n    customer_id\n    loan_purpose\n    payment_amount_cents\n    principal_cents\n    interest_cents\n    late_fee_cents\n    other_fees_cents\n    payment_type\n    payment_status\n    due_date\n    received_date\n    applied_date\n    payment_method\n    principal_balance_after_cents\n    days_past_due_at_payment\n    confirmation_number\n    return_reason_code\n  }\n}\n\n# Every personal loan of the signed-in customer, each with its payment summary.\nquery MyLoans($limit: Int = 20, $offset: Int = 0) @api(mcp: TOOL, rest: GET, uri: \"/my-loans{?limit,offset}\") {\n  CustomerLoans(limit: $limit, offset: $offset) {\n    loan_id\n    customer_id\n    loan_purpose\n    loan_status\n    original_amount_cents\n    current_balance_cents\n    monthly_payment_cents\n    next_payment_due_date\n    applied_payment_count\n    returned_payment_count\n    total_paid_cents\n    principal_paid_cents\n    interest_paid_cents\n    late_fees_paid_cents\n    last_payment_date\n  }\n}\n", "path": "/workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments-api/operations.v1.graphql"}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "together", "model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash", "usage": {"input": 108, "output": 2387, "cacheRead": 142208, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 1057, "totalTokens": 144703, "cost": {"input": 3.24e-05, "output": 0.0028644, "cacheRead": 0.000853248, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.003750048}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1795511038941, "responseId": "027e020c9c9a4f30924ea05df8bfa396-aws_ec1", "rawStopReason": "tool_calls", "durationMs": 5148, "thinkingLevel": "high"}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20ccc42007d019648e5ab", "toolName": "write", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully wrote to /workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments-api/schema.v1.graphqls"}], "isError": false, "durationMs": 4, "timestamp": 1795511044095}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20ccc453f7b628b1894e4", "toolName": "write", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully wrote to /workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments-api/operations.v1.graphql"}], "isError": false, "durationMs": 4, "timestamp": 1795511044095}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "Now mark steps 3 and 4 complete. Then step 6 implement the script (step 5 auth already done). Let me update the plan.\n\nActually step 5 is configure auth \u2014 I already did in the overlays. I'll mark 5 done too. Step 6 implement script.\n\nLet me write the main script now. I'll invoke implement-sqrl skill (already read). Let me write the full script.\n\nConsiderations:\n- `IMPORT data_catalog...` \u2014 the namespace key is `data_catalog`. The skill says relative import from consumer: `IMPORT data_catalog.lending.cards_consumer_credit.consumer_loans-{{environment}} AS cons_loans;`. Good.\n- But the include root is `../data-catalog`. The `consumer_loans-test.sqrl` does `IMPORT consumer_loans.*;` relative to itself. Good.\n\nLet me write the script.\n\nOne concern: `_LatestPersonalLoan` DISTINCT ordered by `source_updated_at DESC`. The requirement FR-2. Good.\n\nAnother: Deduplicating payments: `DISTINCT cons_loans.Loan_Payment ON payment_id ORDER BY source_updated_at DESC`. Then filter `loan_type='PERSONAL'`. Good.\n\n`LoanPaymentsSource` join with latest loans. The requirement says inner join. Good.\n\nAggregation `_AppliedPaymentAgg`: count of APPLIED, sums. Note `late_fees_paid_cents`: sum of late_fee_cents (nullable). `SUM` ignores nulls. `COALESCE(..., 0)` at the summary.\n\nWait, FR-6 says late_fees_paid_cents is sum of late_fee_cents. It doesn't say only nonzero. SUM handles null. Good.\n\nAlso, `principal_paid_cents` sum of principal_cents (nullable). Good.\n\n`returned_payment_count`: count of RETURNED.\n\nNow `LoanPaymentSummarySource` anchored on `_LatestPersonalLoan` left join both aggregations. Good.\n\n`CustomerLoansSource`: join `_LatestPersonalLoan` to `LoanPaymentSummarySource` on loan_id. Actually `LoanPaymentSummarySource` already anchored on `_LatestPersonalLoan`; joining again is redundant but fine. Could just select from `LoanPaymentSummarySource` and add loan details, but summary source doesn't have loan details. So join.\n\nFunctions with claim `customer_id`.\n\nTable tests.\n\nLet me also add `/*+test(no_rows)*/` tests for data integrity:\n- Auto loan leak: `WHERE loan_id LIKE 'AL-%'` \u2014 actually FR-1/FR-3 says no `AL-` loan ids. Since we filter loan_type='PERSONAL' and join latest loans, AL- shouldn't appear.\n- Duplicate payment: group by payment_id HAVING count>1.\n- Duplicate summary loan: group by loan_id HAVING count>1.\n- Row count test.\n\nLet me write.\n\nActually, I realize the `_LatestPersonalLoan` might be considered a VERSIONED_STATE with primary key loan_id. The left join with aggregates. Fine.\n\nLet me write the script.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Steps 3\u20135 are done. Now step 6\u20138: implement the main SQRL script."}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20ccc584d7ad3ac10e73d", "name": "edit", "arguments": {"edits": [{"newText": "- [x] 3. Write the `loan-payments-shared-package.json` base", "oldText": "- [*] 3. Write the `loan-payments-shared-package.json` base"}, {"newText": "- [x] 4. Define the custom GraphQL schema and operations", "oldText": "- [ ] 4. Define the custom GraphQL schema and operations"}, {"newText": "- [x] 5. Configure the Vert.x auth provider", "oldText": "- [ ] 5. Configure the Vert.x auth provider"}, {"newText": "- [*] 6. Implement the `LoanPayments` table", "oldText": "- [ ] 6. Implement the `LoanPayments` table"}], "path": "/workspace/loan-payments/adr/plan_20261124-084455.md"}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20ccc59557be08668f414", "name": "write", "arguments": {"content": "-- Loan Payments API: personal-loan payment history and per-loan summary for customers.\n--\n-- Sources are the shared data-catalog consumer-loan tables. The pipeline owns no data of its own:\n-- it deduplicates the catalog's CDC streams, keeps only personal-loan payments, enriches them from\n-- their loan record, and exposes three lookups that every filter by the caller's customer_id claim.\n\nIMPORT data_catalog.lending.cards_consumer_credit.consumer_loans-{{environment}} AS cons_loans;\n\n-- FR-2: keep the latest version of each loan and payment (CDC streams, at-least-once).\n_LatestPersonalLoan := DISTINCT cons_loans.Personal_Loan ON loan_id ORDER BY source_updated_at DESC;\n_LatestLoanPayment := DISTINCT cons_loans.Loan_Payment ON payment_id ORDER BY source_updated_at DESC;\n\n-- FR-3: only personal-loan payments. Auto-loan payments are out of scope.\n_LatestPersonalLoanPayment :=\n  SELECT * FROM _LatestLoanPayment WHERE loan_type = 'PERSONAL';\n\n-- FR-4, FR-5: one row per payment in every status, enriched with the customer and purpose of the\n-- loan it belongs to. The inner join also enforces that the loan exists in Personal_Loan.\n/*+no_query */\nLoanPaymentsSource :=\n  SELECT p.payment_id,\n         p.loan_id,\n         l.primary_borrower_customer_id AS customer_id,\n         l.loan_purpose,\n         p.payment_amount_cents,\n         p.principal_cents,\n         p.interest_cents,\n         p.late_fee_cents,\n         p.other_fees_cents,\n         p.payment_type,\n         p.payment_status,\n         p.due_date,\n         p.received_date,\n         p.applied_date,\n         p.payment_method,\n         p.principal_balance_after_cents,\n         p.days_past_due_at_payment,\n         p.confirmation_number,\n         p.return_reason_code\n  FROM _LatestPersonalLoanPayment p\n  JOIN _LatestPersonalLoan l ON p.loan_id = l.loan_id;\n\n-- FR-7: only APPLIED payments contribute to the totals and the last payment date.\n_AppliedPaymentAgg :=\n  SELECT loan_id,\n         COUNT(*) AS applied_payment_count,\n         SUM(payment_amount_cents) AS total_paid_cents,\n         SUM(principal_cents) AS principal_paid_cents,\n         SUM(interest_cents) AS interest_paid_cents,\n         SUM(late_fee_cents) AS late_fees_paid_cents,\n         MAX(applied_date) AS last_payment_date\n  FROM LoanPaymentsSource\n  WHERE payment_status = 'APPLIED'\n  GROUP BY loan_id;\n\n_ReturnedPaymentAgg :=\n  SELECT loan_id, COUNT(*) AS returned_payment_count\n  FROM LoanPaymentsSource\n  WHERE payment_status = 'RETURNED'\n  GROUP BY loan_id;\n\n-- FR-6: one row per personal loan, anchored on the latest loans so a loan without payments still\n-- appears with zero counts and sums and a null last payment date.\n/*+no_query */\nLoanPaymentSummarySource :=\n  SELECT l.loan_id,\n         l.primary_borrower_customer_id AS customer_id,\n         l.loan_purpose,\n         COALESCE(a.applied_payment_count, 0) AS applied_payment_count,\n         COALESCE(r.returned_payment_count, 0) AS returned_payment_count,\n         COALESCE(a.total_paid_cents, 0) AS total_paid_cents,\n         COALESCE(a.principal_paid_cents, 0) AS principal_paid_cents,\n         COALESCE(a.interest_paid_cents, 0) AS interest_paid_cents,\n         COALESCE(a.late_fees_paid_cents, 0) AS late_fees_paid_cents,\n         a.last_payment_date\n  FROM _LatestPersonalLoan l\n  LEFT JOIN _AppliedPaymentAgg a ON l.loan_id = a.loan_id\n  LEFT JOIN _ReturnedPaymentAgg r ON l.loan_id = r.loan_id;\n\n-- FR-11: the signed-in customer's loans with their summary and the loan details the client shows.\n/*+no_query */\nCustomerLoansSource :=\n  SELECT l.loan_id,\n         l.primary_borrower_customer_id AS customer_id,\n         l.loan_purpose,\n         l.loan_status,\n         l.original_amount_cents,\n         l.current_balance_cents,\n         l.monthly_payment_cents,\n         l.next_payment_due_date,\n         s.applied_payment_count,\n         s.returned_payment_count,\n         s.total_paid_cents,\n         s.principal_paid_cents,\n         s.interest_paid_cents,\n         s.late_fees_paid_cents,\n         s.last_payment_date\n  FROM _LatestPersonalLoan l\n  JOIN LoanPaymentSummarySource s ON l.loan_id = s.loan_id;\n\n-- FR-9, FR-12: summary of one loan, filtered by the JWT claim so another customer's loan is invisible.\nLoanPaymentSummary(loan_id STRING NOT NULL, customer_id STRING NOT NULL METADATA FROM 'auth.customer_id') :=\n  SELECT * FROM LoanPaymentSummarySource\n  WHERE loan_id = :loan_id AND customer_id = :customer_id;\n\n-- FR-10, FR-12: payments of one loan, newest due date first, same claim filter.\nLoanPayments(loan_id STRING NOT NULL, customer_id STRING NOT NULL METADATA FROM 'auth.customer_id') :=\n  SELECT * FROM LoanPaymentsSource\n  WHERE loan_id = :loan_id AND customer_id = :customer_id\n  ORDER BY due_date DESC, payment_id;\n\n-- FR-11, FR-12: every personal loan of the signed-in customer, each with its summary.\nCustomerLoans(customer_id STRING NOT NULL METADATA FROM 'auth.customer_id') :=\n  SELECT * FROM CustomerLoansSource\n  WHERE customer_id = :customer_id\n  ORDER BY loan_id;\n\n/* ==== TABLE TESTS (run by loan-payments-table-test-package.json against the inferred schema) ==== */\n\n-- FR-1, FR-3: exactly the 1,010 personal payments remain; no auto-loan payment leaked in.\n/*+test */\nLoanPaymentsCountTest :=\n  SELECT COUNT(*) AS payment_rows, COUNT(DISTINCT loan_id) AS loans_with_payments\n  FROM LoanPaymentsSource;\n\n/*+test(no_rows) */\nAutoLoanLeakTest :=\n  SELECT * FROM LoanPaymentsSource WHERE loan_id LIKE 'AL-%';\n\n-- FR-2: one row per payment_id and one row per loan_id.\n/*+test(no_rows) */\nDuplicateLoanPaymentsTest :=\n  SELECT payment_id, COUNT(*) AS num_rows\n  FROM LoanPaymentsSource GROUP BY payment_id HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;\n\n/*+test(no_rows) */\nDuplicateLoanSummaryTest :=\n  SELECT loan_id, COUNT(*) AS num_rows\n  FROM LoanPaymentSummarySource GROUP BY loan_id HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;\n\n-- FR-6: a loan without payments has zero counts and sums and a null last payment date.\n/*+test */\nZeroPaymentSummaryTest :=\n  SELECT loan_id, applied_payment_count, returned_payment_count, total_paid_cents, last_payment_date\n  FROM LoanPaymentSummarySource WHERE loan_id = 'PL-011';\n", "path": "/workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments.sqrl"}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "together", "model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash", "usage": {"input": 127, "output": 2620, "cacheRead": 144640, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 672, "totalTokens": 147387, "cost": {"input": 3.81e-05, "output": 0.0031439999999999997, "cacheRead": 0.00086784, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.00404994}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "time