is the one for JWT auth. Let me look at it. Let me find the exact auth patterns. Let me read the user_analytics project and docs.\n+00:00:10  TOOL   bash find /opt/datasqrl-examples/user_analytics -type f | grep -v build | sort\n+00:00:10  TOOL   read /opt/datasqrl-examples/user_analytics/README.md\n+00:00:12  THINK  This is the key example. Let me read the user_analytics main sqrl, test package, prod package, shared package, and test files/properties, and run-tests.sh.\n"}], "isError": false, "durationMs": 16, "timestamp": 1795511105641}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "The context says \"Compile/test from the project \u2014 the package path is resolved at the mount root, so it must be project-qualified: /opt/agent/cmd.sh compile loan-payments/<your>-package.json\". This suggests no `-r` and the config path includes `loan-payments/`. But the standard run-tests.sh uses `-r` and unprefixed configs.\n\nThe harness likely sets SQRL_PACKAGE_PREFIX when running run-tests.sh as the final command. Since the task says the last action is `./run-tests.sh`, and the harness is designed around the template, I'll trust that SQRL_PACKAGE_PREFIX=loan-payments/ is exported at final run. But when I run it now for verification, it's not set, so `-r .` would be wrong.\n\nLet me test: temporarily run `SQRL_PACKAGE_PREFIX=loan-payments/ ./run-tests.sh --compile --env prod loan-payments` maybe. Or set it inline for my runs. But my final line must be bare `./run-tests.sh` (the harness runs it). Actually, my \"last action\" is the command I output as the final line; the harness will execute it. It likely executes in an environment where SQRL_PACKAGE_PREFIX is set. Let me verify by checking the datasqrl-agent-context or the harness. Hmm.\n\nActually, the final line is what `./run-tests.sh` I want the harness to run. The harness presumably runs it with the proper env (SQRL_PACKAGE_PREFIX). The instructions say \"Output that exact invocation as your final li