T=\".\" and `/workspace/<project>` ... hmm, the script doesn't know the project path. But `HOST_WORKSPACE_FOLDER` env var is available! I could use it as a fallback. But the template says keep everything else unchanged. Adding a fallback would deviate. Hmm.\n\nActually, the template's P branch is exactly for the DataSQRL agent container. The harness sets SQRL_PACKAGE_PREFIX. I'll leave as is.\n\nLet me now do the final run-tests.sh with SQRL_PACKAGE_PREFIX set. But the instructions say the final line must be the bare command `./run-tests.sh`. The harness will run it. I'll run it myself with the prefix for verification, then output the bare command as my final line.\n\nActually, the instruction: \"Your last action must be a successful run of `./run-tests.sh`... Output that exact invocation as your final line\". So my final message ends with `./run-tests.sh`. I should ensure it passes. I already ran it successfully. But I've since modified README (no effect) and compiled prod (overwrote build/loan-payments with prod artifacts). The next test run will recompile test config, so fine. Let me do one final clean run to be safe.\n\nActually, there's a risk: the prod compile overwrote `build/loan-payments`. The test run will rebuild. Fine.\n\nLet me run the final `./run-tests.sh` with SQRL_PACKAGE_PREFIX. This is the last action. Let me run and confirm exit 0.\n\nWait, but the final action required is \"running the tests successfully\" and the last line is the bare command. I'll run it now and then output the bare command. Let me run with the prefix.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "text", "text": "All plan steps are complete. Let me do the final verification run of the full test suite."}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20ccfca5f744296de558d", "name": "bash", "arguments": {"command": "cd /workspace/loan-payments && SQRL_PACKAGE_PREFIX=loan-payments/ ./run-tests.sh > /tmp/loanpay_final.log 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\"; grep -E \"Tests run|BUILD SUCCESS|BU