{"request_uuid": "a5a0a341-67dd-4fe9-88b6-c2c5702db363", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T09:12:06.629246+00:00", "level": "INFO", "mode": "implementation", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "source": "judge", "message": "Judge pipeline: 13 issue(s)", "name": "pipeline", "issue_count": 13, "issues": [{"severity": "HIGH", "description": "_AppliedPaymentAgg uses a global, non-windowed GROUP BY aggregation with MAX(applied_date). MAX is a non-incremental aggregation function; on a retract stream this can cause unbounded state growth. Consider using an upstream time-window or aggregating in the database if state can be large.", "location": "Pipeline Definition", "verifier": "pipeline"}, {"severity": "MEDIUM", "description": "State table CustomerLoansSource has no valid event timestamp (Timestamp: -).", "location": "Pipeline Definition", "verifier": "pipeline"}, {"severity": "MEDIUM", "description": "State table LoanPaymentSummarySource has no valid event timestamp (Timestamp: -).", "location": "Pipeline Definition", "verifier": "pipeline"}, {"severity": "MEDIUM", "description": "State table LoanPaymentsSource has no valid event timestamp (Timestamp: -).", "location": "Pipeline Definition", "verifier": "pipeline"}, {"severity": "MEDIUM", "description": "State table _AppliedPaymentAgg has no valid event timestamp (Timestamp: -).", "location": "Pipeline Definition", "verifier": "pipeline"}, {"severity": "MEDIUM", "description": "State table _ReturnedPaymentAgg has no valid event timestamp (Timestamp: -).", "location": "Pipeline Definition", "verifier": "pipeline"}, {"severity": "MEDIUM", "description": "CustomerLoansSource is a Flink state table with a stateful join between _LatestPersonalLoan and LoanPaymentSummarySource on loan_id; this may accumulate state over time.", "location": "Pipeline Definition", "verifier": "pipeline"}, {"severity": "MEDIUM", "description": "LoanPaymentSummarySource is a Flink state table with stateful LEFT JOINs between _LatestPersonalLoan and the payment aggregation tables; this may accumulate state over time.", "location": "Pipeline Definition", "verifier": "pipeline"}, {"severity": "MEDIUM", "description": "LoanPaymentsSource is a Flink state table with a stateful join between _LatestPersonalLoanPayment and _LatestPersonalLoan on loan_id; this may accumulate state over time.", "location": "Pipeline Definition", "verifier": "pipeline"}, {"severity": "MEDIUM", "description": "_AppliedPaymentAgg is a Flink state table with a high-cardinality GROUP BY loan_id aggregation; this may accumulate state over time.", "location": "Pipeline Definition", "verifier": "pipeline"}, {"severity": "MEDIUM", "description": "_ReturnedPaymentAgg is a Flink state table with a high-cardinality GROUP BY loan_id aggregation; this may accumulate state over time.", "location": "Pipeline Definition", "verifier": "pipeline"}, {"severity": "LOW", "description": "Stateful joins/aggregations in CustomerLoansSource, LoanPaymentSummarySource, LoanPaymentsSource, _AppliedPaymentAgg, and _ReturnedPaymentAgg could potentially be rewritten with time bounds (interval join, temporal join, or time-window aggregation) to reduce state accumulation, if the original requirements and semantics allow it.", "location": "Pipeline Definition", "verifier": "pipeline"}, {"severity": "LOW", "description": "Pipeline has no data quality (DQ_) or observability statistics (OB_) tables, nor tables with equivalent purpose by naming/definition/comments.", "location": "Pipeline Definition", "verifier": "pipeline"}], "cost_usd": 0.0125592, "duration_ms": 15233}
{"request_uuid": "a5a0a341-67dd-4fe9-88b6-c2c5702db363", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T09:12:08.632264+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "implementation", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "source": "judge", "name": "tests", "prompt": "# DataSQRL Test Review\n\nDataSQRL compiles SQL code (the dialect is called SQRL and an extension of Flink SQL 2.3 with additional support for IMPORT/EXPORT statements, table functions, and relationship) to integrated data pipelines that execute from source to sink using engines like Apache Flink, Postgres, Kafka, Apache Iceberg, DuckDB and others.\nThe DataSQRL framework supports testing by creating snapshots of the results of table definitions annotated with the `/*+test */` hint or executing test queries as GraphQL queries.\n\nGiven the SQRL code below, identify whether the tests defined therein provide sufficient test coverage for the table and function definitions. Ignore tables starting with an underscore `_`. Consider that non-deterministic tables (like generated data) and columns (like timestamps) should be excluded from tests. Consider tables to be sufficiently covered if downstream tables or functions have tests.\nProduce issues for any identified test coverage gap with severity: LOW.\n\nAlso review the project's test runner script when one is shown below. It is the project's whole\ntest process \u2014 the single command the coding agent, CI and the user run. Judge whether its\ninventory is complete and reproducible:\n\n- Every sub-project's suite is invoked (one entry per sub-project in the `suite` table, run with `-b <sub>`). A suite the script never invokes is silently untested \u2014 severity MEDIUM\n- Every suite invocation names its own build folder (`-b <sub-project>`, which resolves to `build/<sub-project>`). Without `-b`  or `--build` flag, every suite writes to `build/` dir by default and overwrites the previous one, so the review sees only the last \u2014 severity MEDIUM.\n- The setup it performs (test-data generation or download, fixtures) makes the run reproducible\n  from a clean checkout; a suite that depends on data the script does not produce or fetch is a\n  coverage gap \u2014 severity LOW.\n- Every selected suite runs even after one fails, and the script exits non-zero when any failed.\n  A `set -e` before the suite lines, or a suite whose failure is swallowed, hides the other\n  failures \u2014 severity LOW.\n\nSelecting suites by argument (`selected <sub> && \u2026`, `./run-tests.sh <sub>`) is the intended\ndesign and is not an issue; the inventory is what must be complete.\n\n## SQRL Code\n```\nCREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS `cons_loans`;\nUSE `cons_loans`;\n/** Personal/unsecured loan records.\n    Grain: one row per loan_id.\n\n    # Columns:\n    * loan_id: Unique identifier for the loan\n    * application_id: Reference to application\n    * primary_borrower_customer_id: Reference to primary borrower @pii\n    * loan_number: Loan number displayed to customer @npi @mask\n    * loan_status: Loan status: ACTIVE, PAID_OFF, CHARGED_OFF, SETTLED\n    * loan_purpose: Loan purpose: DEBT_CONSOLIDATION, HOME_IMPROVEMENT, MAJOR_PURCHASE, MEDICAL, VACATION, OTHER\n    * original_amount_cents: Original loan amount in cents @npi @confidential\n    * current_balance_cents: Current principal balance in cents @npi @confidential\n    * interest_rate: Interest rate (APR) @confidential\n    * rate_type: Rate type: FIXED, VARIABLE\n    * original_term_months: Original term in months\n    * remaining_term_months: Remaining term in months\n    * monthly_payment_cents: Monthly payment amount in cents @npi @confidential\n    * funding_date: Date loan was funded\n    * first_payment_date: First payment due date\n    * maturity_date: Maturity date\n    * next_payment_due_date: Next payment due date\n    * paid_off_date: Date loan was paid off\n    * origination_fee_cents: Origination fee in cents\n    * credit_score_at_origination: Credit score at origination @npi @confidential\n    * dti_at_origination: DTI ratio at origination @npi @confidential\n    * autopay_enrolled: Autopay enrolled\n    * disbursement_account_id: Disbursement account @npi\n    * payment_account_id: Payment account @npi\n    * origination_channel: Origination channel: ONLINE, BRANCH, PHONE, PARTNER\n    * source_system: Source system identifier\n    * source_updated_at: Timestamp when record was last updated in source system */\nCREATE TABLE Personal_Loan_schema (\n  loan_id STRING NOT NULL,\n  application_id STRING,\n  primary_borrower_customer_id STRING NOT NULL,\n  loan_number STRING NOT NULL,\n  loan_status STRING NOT NULL,\n  loan_purpose STRING,\n  original_amount_cents BIGINT NOT NULL,\n  current_balance_cents BIGINT NOT NULL,\n  interest_rate DECIMAL(6, 4) NOT NULL,\n  rate_type STRING NOT NULL,\n  original_term_months INT NOT NULL,\n  remaining_term_months INT,\n  monthly_payment_cents BIGINT NOT NULL,\n  funding_date DATE NOT NULL,\n  first_payment_date DATE NOT NULL,\n  maturity_date DATE NOT NULL,\n  next_payment_due_date DATE,\n  paid_off_date DATE,\n  origination_fee_cents BIGINT,\n  credit_score_at_origination INT,\n  dti_at_origination DECIMAL(5, 2),\n  autopay_enrolled BOOLEAN NOT NULL,\n  disbursement_account_id STRING,\n  payment_account_id STRING,\n  origination_channel STRING,\n  source_system STRING NOT NULL,\n  source_updated_at TIMESTAMP_LTZ(3) NOT NULL\n);\n/** Auto loan records with vehicle collateral information.\n    Grain: one row per loan_id.\n\n    # Columns:\n    * loan_id: Unique identifier for the loan\n    * application_id: Reference to application\n    * primary_borrower_customer_id: Reference to primary borrower @pii\n    * loan_number: Loan number displayed to customer @npi @mask\n    * loan_status: Loan status: ACTIVE, PAID_OFF, CHARGED_OFF, REPOSSESSED\n    * loan_type: Loan type: NEW_VEHICLE, USED_VEHICLE, REFINANCE, LEASE_BUYOUT\n    * original_amount_cents: Original loan amount in cents @npi @confidential\n    * current_balance_cents: Current principal balance in cents @npi @confidential\n    * interest_rate: Interest rate (APR) @confidential\n    * rate_type: Rate type: FIXED, VARIABLE\n    * original_term_months: Original term in months\n    * remaining_term_months: Remaining term in months\n    * monthly_payment_cents: Monthly payment amount in cents @npi @confidential\n    * funding_date: Date loan was funded\n    * first_payment_date: First payment due date\n    * maturity_date: Maturity date\n    * next_payment_due_date: Next payment due date\n    * paid_off_date: Date loan was paid off\n    * vehicle_vin: Vehicle VIN @pii\n    * vehicle_year: Vehicle year\n    * vehicle_make: Vehicle make\n    * vehicle_model: Vehicle model\n    * vehicle_trim: Vehicle trim\n    * mileage_at_origination: Vehicle mileage at origination\n    * vehicle_condition: Vehicle condition: NEW, USED, CERTIFIED\n    * vehicle_value_at_origination_cents: Vehicle value at origination in cents @npi @confidential\n    * current_vehicle_value_cents: Current estimated vehicle value in cents @npi @confidential\n    * ltv_at_origination: Loan-to-value ratio at origination\n    * current_ltv: Current LTV\n    * dealer_name: Dealer name @pii\n    * dealer_id: Dealer ID\n    * gap_insurance: GAP insurance included\n    * extended_warranty: Extended warranty included\n    * credit_score_at_origination: Credit score at origination @npi @confidential\n    * dti_at_origination: DTI ratio at origination @npi @confidential\n    * title_status: Title status: HELD, RELEASED, DEFECTIVE\n    * lien_state: Lien holder state\n    * autopay_enrolled: Autopay enrolled\n    * source_system: Source system identifier\n    * source_updated_at: Timestamp when record was last updated in source system */\nCREATE TABLE Auto_Loan_schema (\n  loan_id STRING NOT NULL,\n  application_id STRING,\n  primary_borrower_customer_id STRING NOT NULL,\n  loan_number STRING NOT NULL,\n  loan_status STRING NOT NULL,\n  loan_type STRING NOT NULL,\n  original_amount_cents BIGINT NOT NULL,\n  current_balance_cents BIGINT NOT NULL,\n  interest_rate DECIMAL(6, 4) NOT NULL,\n  rate_type STRING NOT NULL,\n  original_term_months INT NOT NULL,\n  remaining_term_months INT,\n  monthly_payment_cents BIGINT NOT NULL,\n  funding_date DATE NOT NULL,\n  first_payment_date DATE NOT NULL,\n  maturity_date DATE NOT NULL,\n  next_payment_due_date DATE,\n  paid_off_date DATE,\n  vehicle_vin STRING NOT NULL,\n  vehicle_year INT NOT NULL,\n  vehicle_make STRING NOT NULL,\n  vehicle_model STRING NOT NULL,\n  vehicle_trim STRING,\n  mileage_at_origination INT,\n  vehicle_condition STRING NOT NULL,\n  vehicle_value_at_origination_cents BIGINT,\n  current_vehicle_value_cents BIGINT,\n  ltv_at_origination DECIMAL(5, 2),\n  current_ltv DECIMAL(5, 2),\n  dealer_name STRING,\n  dealer_id STRING,\n  gap_insurance BOOLEAN,\n  extended_warranty BOOLEAN,\n  credit_score_at_origination INT,\n  dti_at_origination DECIMAL(5, 2),\n  title_status STRING,\n  lien_state STRING,\n  autopay_enrolled BOOLEAN NOT NULL,\n  source_system STRING NOT NULL,\n  source_updated_at TIMESTAMP_LTZ(3) NOT NULL\n);\n/** Consumer loan payment records (personal and auto).\n    Grain: one row per payment_id.\n\n    # Columns:\n    * payment_id: Unique identifier for the payment\n    * loan_id: Reference to loan\n    * loan_type: Loan type: PERSONAL, AUTO\n    * payment_amount_cents: Payment amount in cents @npi @confidential\n    * principal_cents: Principal portion in cents @npi @confidential\n    * interest_cents: Interest portion in cents @npi @confidential\n    * late_fee_cents: Late fee amount in cents\n    * other_fees_cents: Other fees in cents\n    * payment_type: Payment type: REGULAR, EXTRA_PRINCIPAL, PAYOFF, PARTIAL\n    * payment_status: Payment status: APPLIED, PENDING, RETURNED, REVERSED\n    * due_date: Date payment was due\n    * received_date: Date payment was received\n    * applied_date: Date payment was applied\n    * payment_method: Payment method: ACH, CHECK, DEBIT_CARD, ONLINE\n    * principal_balance_after_cents: Principal balance after payment in cents @npi @confidential\n    * days_past_due_at_payment: Days past due at time of payment\n    * confirmation_number: Confirmation number\n    * return_reason_code: Return reason code (if returned)\n    * source_system: Source system identifier\n    * source_updated_at: Timestamp when record was last updated in source system */\nCREATE TABLE Loan_Payment_schema (\n  payment_id STRING NOT NULL,\n  loan_id STRING NOT NULL,\n  loan_type STRING NOT NULL,\n  payment_amount_cents BIGINT NOT NULL,\n  principal_cents BIGINT,\n  interest_cents BIGINT,\n  late_fee_cents BIGINT,\n  other_fees_cents BIGINT,\n  payment_type STRING NOT NULL,\n  payment_status STRING NOT NULL,\n  due_date DATE NOT NULL,\n  received_date DATE,\n  applied_date DATE,\n  payment_method STRING,\n  principal_balance_after_cents BIGINT,\n  days_past_due_at_payment INT,\n  confirmation_number STRING,\n  return_reason_code STRING,\n  source_system STRING NOT NULL,\n  source_updated_at TIMESTAMP_LTZ(3) NOT NULL\n);\n/** Consumer loan application records.\n    Grain: one row per application_id.\n\n    # Columns:\n    * application_id: Unique identifier for the application\n    * primary_applicant_customer_id: Reference to primary applicant @pii\n    * co_applicant_customer_id: Reference to co-applicant (if applicable) @pii\n    * loan_type: Loan type: PERSONAL, AUTO\n    * loan_purpose: Loan purpose: DEBT_CONSOLIDATION, HOME_IMPROVEMENT, VEHICLE_PURCHASE, REFINANCE, OTHER\n    * requested_amount_cents: Requested loan amount in cents @npi @confidential\n    * requested_term_months: Requested term in months\n    * application_status: Application status: SUBMITTED, IN_REVIEW, APPROVED, COUNTER_OFFER, DENIED, WITHDRAWN, FUNDED\n    * submitted_at: Date application was submitted\n    * decision_date: Date decision was made\n    * decision_type: Decision type: APPROVED, DENIED, COUNTER_OFFER\n    * approved_amount_cents: Approved amount in cents @npi @confidential\n    * approved_rate: Approved rate @confidential\n    * approved_term_months: Approved term in months\n    * denial_reasons: Denial reason codes (if denied) @confidential\n    * credit_score: Credit score at application @npi @confidential\n    * annual_income_cents: Annual income stated @npi @confidential\n    * monthly_debt_cents: Monthly debt obligations @npi @confidential\n    * dti_ratio: DTI ratio calculated @npi @confidential\n    * employment_status: Employment status: EMPLOYED, SELF_EMPLOYED, RETIRED, OTHER\n    * employer_name: Employer name @pii\n    * years_employed: Years at current employer\n    * origination_channel: Origination channel: ONLINE, BRANCH, PHONE, DEALER, PARTNER\n    * promo_code: Promo code applied\n    * funded_date: Date application was funded\n    * source_system: Source system identifier\n    * source_updated_at: Timestamp when record was last updated in source system */\nCREATE TABLE Loan_Application_schema (\n  application_id STRING NOT NULL,\n  primary_applicant_customer_id STRING NOT NULL,\n  co_applicant_customer_id STRING,\n  loan_type STRING NOT NULL,\n  loan_purpose STRING,\n  requested_amount_cents BIGINT NOT NULL,\n  requested_term_months INT,\n  application_status STRING NOT NULL,\n  submitted_at TIMESTAMP_LTZ(3) NOT NULL,\n  decision_date DATE,\n  decision_type STRING,\n  approved_amount_cents BIGINT,\n  approved_rate DECIMAL(6, 4),\n  approved_term_months INT,\n  denial_reasons STRING,\n  credit_score INT,\n  annual_income_cents BIGINT,\n  monthly_debt_cents BIGINT,\n  dti_ratio DECIMAL(5, 2),\n  employment_status STRING,\n  employer_name STRING,\n  years_employed INT,\n  origination_channel STRING,\n  promo_code STRING,\n  funded_date DATE,\n  source_system STRING NOT NULL,\n  source_updated_at TIMESTAMP_LTZ(3) NOT NULL\n);\n/** Consumer loan delinquency events.\n    Grain: one row per delinquency_event_id.\n\n    # Columns:\n    * delinquency_event_id: Unique identifier for the delinquency event\n    * loan_id: Reference to loan\n    * loan_type: Loan type: PERSONAL, AUTO\n    * customer_id: Reference to customer @pii\n    * event_type: Event type: MISSED_PAYMENT, DELINQUENCY_START, DELINQUENCY_CURED, CHARGE_OFF, REPOSSESSION, COLLECTION_ASSIGNED, RECOVERY\n    * days_past_due: Days past due at event\n    * delinquency_bucket: Delinquency bucket: CURRENT, 30_DAY, 60_DAY, 90_DAY, 120_PLUS\n    * amount_past_due_cents: Amount past due in cents @npi @confidential\n    * total_balance_cents: Total balance at event in cents @npi @confidential\n    * event_date: Event date\n    * cured_date: Date cured (if applicable)\n    * collection_action: Collection action taken @confidential\n    * collection_agency: Collection agency assigned\n    * repossession_date: Repossession date (for auto)\n    * repossession_agency: Repossession agency\n    * sale_date: Sale date (for repo)\n    * sale_amount_cents: Sale amount in cents\n    * deficiency_balance_cents: Deficiency balance in cents @npi @confidential\n    * charge_off_date: Charge-off date\n    * charge_off_amount_cents: Charge-off amount in cents @npi @confidential\n    * recovery_amount_cents: Recovery amount in cents\n    * source_system: Source system identifier\n    * source_updated_at: Timestamp when record was last updated in source system */\nCREATE TABLE Consumer_Loan_Delinquency_Event_schema (\n  delinquency_event_id STRING NOT NULL,\n  loan_id STRING NOT NULL,\n  loan_type STRING NOT NULL,\n  customer_id STRING NOT NULL,\n  event_type STRING NOT NULL,\n  days_past_due INT NOT NULL,\n  delinquency_bucket STRING NOT NULL,\n  amount_past_due_cents BIGINT,\n  total_balance_cents BIGINT,\n  event_date DATE NOT NULL,\n  cured_date DATE,\n  collection_action STRING,\n  collection_agency STRING,\n  repossession_date DATE,\n  repossession_agency STRING,\n  sale_date DATE,\n  sale_amount_cents BIGINT,\n  deficiency_balance_cents BIGINT,\n  charge_off_date DATE,\n  charge_off_amount_cents BIGINT,\n  recovery_amount_cents BIGINT,\n  source_system STRING NOT NULL,\n  source_updated_at TIMESTAMP_LTZ(3) NOT NULL\n);\nCREATE TABLE Personal_Loan (\n  /** Timestamp when record was ingested into the data platform */\n  ingested_at TIMESTAMP_LTZ(3) METADATA FROM 'timestamp',\n  WATERMARK FOR ingested_at AS ingested_at - INTERVAL '30' SECOND\n) WITH (\n    'connector' = 'kafka-safe',\n    'properties.bootstrap.servers' = '${LENDING_KAFKA_BROKERS}',\n    'properties.group.id' = '${DEPLOYMENT_ID}',\n    'topic' = 'consumer_loans.personal_loan',\n    'scan.startup.mode' = 'earliest-offset',\n    'value.format' = 'json',\n    'value.json.timestamp-format.standard' = 'ISO-8601'\n) LIKE Personal_Loan_schema;\nCREATE TABLE Auto_Loan (\n  /** Timestamp when record was ingested into the data platform */\n  ingested_at TIMESTAMP_LTZ(3) METADATA FROM 'timestamp',\n  WATERMARK FOR ingested_at AS ingested_at - INTERVAL '30' SECOND\n) WITH (\n    'connector' = 'kafka-safe',\n    'properties.bootstrap.servers' = '${LENDING_KAFKA_BROKERS}',\n    'properties.group.id' = '${DEPLOYMENT_ID}',\n    'topic' = 'consumer_loans.auto_loan',\n    'scan.startup.mode' = 'earliest-offset',\n    'value.format' = 'json',\n    'value.json.timestamp-format.standard' = 'ISO-8601'\n) LIKE Auto_Loan_schema;\nCREATE TABLE Loan_Payment (\n  /** Timestamp when record was ingested into the data platform */\n  ingested_at TIMESTAMP_LTZ(3) METADATA FROM 'timestamp',\n  WATERMARK FOR ingested_at AS ingested_at - INTERVAL '30' SECOND\n) WITH (\n    'connector' = 'kafka-safe',\n    'properties.bootstrap.servers' = '${LENDING_KAFKA_BROKERS}',\n    'properties.group.id' = '${DEPLOYMENT_ID}',\n    'topic' = 'consumer_loans.loan_payment',\n    'scan.startup.mode' = 'earliest-offset',\n    'value.format' = 'json',\n    'value.json.timestamp-format.standard' = 'ISO-8601'\n) LIKE Loan_Payment_schema;\nCREATE TABLE Loan_Application (\n  /** Timestamp when record was ingested into the data platform */\n  ingested_at TIMESTAMP_LTZ(3) METADATA FROM 'timestamp',\n  WATERMARK FOR ingested_at AS ingested_at - INTERVAL '30' SECOND\n) WITH (\n    'connector' = 'kafka-safe',\n    'properties.bootstrap.servers' = '${LENDING_KAFKA_BROKERS}',\n    'properties.group.id' = '${DEPLOYMENT_ID}',\n    'topic' = 'consumer_loans.loan_application',\n    'scan.startup.mode' = 'earliest-offset',\n    'value.format' = 'json',\n    'value.json.timestamp-format.standard' = 'ISO-8601'\n) LIKE Loan_Application_schema;\nCREATE TABLE Consumer_Loan_Delinquency_Event (\n  /** Timestamp when record was ingested into the data platform */\n  ingested_at TIMESTAMP_LTZ(3) METADATA FROM 'timestamp',\n  WATERMARK FOR ingested_at AS ingested_at - INTERVAL '30' SECOND\n) WITH (\n    'connector' = 'kafka-safe',\n    'properties.bootstrap.servers' = '${LENDING_KAFKA_BROKERS}',\n    'properties.group.id' = '${DEPLOYMENT_ID}',\n    'topic' = 'consumer_loans.consumer_loan_delinquency_event',\n    'scan.startup.mode' = 'earliest-offset',\n    'value.format' = 'json',\n    'value.json.timestamp-format.standard' = 'ISO-8601'\n) LIKE Consumer_Loan_Delinquency_Event_schema;\nUSE CATALOG `default_catalog`;\nCREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS `default_database`;\nUSE `default_database`;\n_LatestPersonalLoan := DISTINCT cons_loans.Personal_Loan ON loan_id ORDER BY source_updated_at DESC;\n_LatestLoanPayment := DISTINCT cons_loans.Loan_Payment ON payment_id ORDER BY source_updated_at DESC;\n_LatestPersonalLoanPayment :=\n  SELECT * FROM _LatestLoanPayment WHERE loan_type = 'PERSONAL';\n/*+no_query */\nLoanPaymentsSource :=\n  SELECT p.payment_id,\n         p.loan_id,\n         l.primary_borrower_customer_id AS customer_id,\n         l.loan_purpose,\n         p.payment_amount_cents,\n         p.principal_cents,\n         p.interest_cents,\n         p.late_fee_cents,\n         p.other_fees_cents,\n         p.payment_type,\n         p.payment_status,\n         p.due_date,\n         p.received_date,\n         p.applied_date,\n         p.payment_method,\n         p.principal_balance_after_cents,\n         p.days_past_due_at_payment,\n         p.confirmation_number,\n         p.return_reason_code\n  FROM _LatestPersonalLoanPayment p\n  JOIN _LatestPersonalLoan l ON p.loan_id = l.loan_id;\n_AppliedPaymentAgg :=\n  SELECT loan_id,\n         COUNT(*) AS applied_payment_count,\n         SUM(payment_amount_cents) AS total_paid_cents,\n         SUM(principal_cents) AS principal_paid_cents,\n         SUM(interest_cents) AS interest_paid_cents,\n         SUM(late_fee_cents) AS late_fees_paid_cents,\n         MAX(applied_date) AS last_payment_date\n  FROM LoanPaymentsSource\n  WHERE payment_status = 'APPLIED'\n  GROUP BY loan_id;\n_ReturnedPaymentAgg :=\n  SELECT loan_id, COUNT(*) AS returned_payment_count\n  FROM LoanPaymentsSource\n  WHERE payment_status = 'RETURNED'\n  GROUP BY loan_id;\n/*+no_query */\nLoanPaymentSummarySource :=\n  SELECT l.loan_id,\n         l.primary_borrower_customer_id AS customer_id,\n         l.loan_purpose,\n         COALESCE(a.applied_payment_count, 0) AS applied_payment_count,\n         COALESCE(r.returned_payment_count, 0) AS returned_payment_count,\n         COALESCE(a.total_paid_cents, 0) AS total_paid_cents,\n         COALESCE(a.principal_paid_cents, 0) AS principal_paid_cents,\n         COALESCE(a.interest_paid_cents, 0) AS interest_paid_cents,\n         COALESCE(a.late_fees_paid_cents, 0) AS late_fees_paid_cents,\n         a.last_payment_date\n  FROM _LatestPersonalLoan l\n  LEFT JOIN _AppliedPaymentAgg a ON l.loan_id = a.loan_id\n  LEFT JOIN _ReturnedPaymentAgg r ON l.loan_id = r.loan_id;\n/*+no_query */\nCustomerLoansSource :=\n  SELECT l.loan_id,\n         l.primary_borrower_customer_id AS customer_id,\n         l.loan_purpose,\n         l.loan_status,\n         l.original_amount_cents,\n         l.current_balance_cents,\n         l.monthly_payment_cents,\n         l.next_payment_due_date,\n         s.applied_payment_count,\n         s.returned_payment_count,\n         s.total_paid_cents,\n         s.principal_paid_cents,\n         s.interest_paid_cents,\n         s.late_fees_paid_cents,\n         s.last_payment_date\n  FROM _LatestPersonalLoan l\n  JOIN LoanPaymentSummarySource s ON l.loan_id = s.loan_id;\nLoanPaymentSummary(loan_id STRING NOT NULL, customer_id STRING NOT NULL METADATA FROM 'auth.customer_id') :=\n  SELECT * FROM LoanPaymentSummarySource\n  WHERE loan_id = :loan_id AND customer_id = :customer_id;\nLoanPayments(loan_id STRING NOT NULL, customer_id STRING NOT NULL METADATA FROM 'auth.customer_id') :=\n  SELECT * FROM LoanPaymentsSource\n  WHERE loan_id = :loan_id AND customer_id = :customer_id\n  ORDER BY due_date DESC, payment_id;\nCustomerLoans(customer_id STRING NOT NULL METADATA FROM 'auth.customer_id') :=\n  SELECT * FROM CustomerLoansSource\n  WHERE customer_id = :customer_id\n  ORDER BY loan_id;\n/* ==== TABLE TESTS (run by loan-payments-table-test-package.json against the inferred schema) ==== */\n\n\n/*+test */\nLoanPaymentsCountTest :=\n  SELECT COUNT(*) AS payment_rows, COUNT(DISTINCT loan_id) AS loans_with_payments\n  FROM LoanPaymentsSource;\n/*+test(no_rows) */\nAutoLoanLeakTest :=\n  SELECT * FROM LoanPaymentsSource WHERE loan_id LIKE 'AL-%';\n/*+test(no_rows) */\nDuplicateLoanPaymentsTest :=\n  SELECT payment_id, COUNT(*) AS num_rows\n  FROM LoanPaymentsSource GROUP BY payment_id HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;\n/*+test(no_rows) */\nDuplicateLoanSummaryTest :=\n  SELECT loan_id, COUNT(*) AS num_rows\n  FROM LoanPaymentSummarySource GROUP BY loan_id HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;\n/*+test */\nZeroPaymentSummaryTest :=\n  SELECT loan_id, applied_payment_count, returned_payment_count, total_paid_cents, last_payment_date\n  FROM LoanPaymentSummarySource WHERE loan_id = 'PL-011';\n\n```\n\n### Test Runner Script (run-tests.sh)\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# This project's suites \u2014 one command, deterministic exit code.\n# Used by the DataSQRL agent and by CI.\n#\n# USAGE\n#   ./run-tests.sh [options] [<sub-project> ...]\n#\n#   <sub-project>       zero or more names, in any order, selecting which suites run.\n#                       Give none to run them all. Options may appear before, after or\n#                       between the names.\n#\n#   --compile           compile instead of running tests\n#   --test              run tests (the default)\n#   --env <name>        which environment's configs to use (default: test).\n#                       `--env=<name>` is accepted too.\n#   --list-envs         print the environments this project declares, one line\n#   --list-subprojects  print the sub-projects this project ships, one line\n#   --list-invocations  print what would run and run nothing, one\n#                       `SQRL_INVOCATION <sub-project> <verb> -r <root> <config...> -b <name>`\n#                       line per suite \u2014 exactly the arguments a real run would use\n#\n# EXAMPLES (using this project's own sub-project, event_audit)\n#   ./run-tests.sh                                     test every suite, env test\n#   ./run-tests.sh event_audit                         test just that sub-project\n#   ./run-tests.sh --compile --env dev                 compile every suite as dev\n#   ./run-tests.sh --compile --env prod event_audit    compile just that one, as prod\n#   ./run-tests.sh --list-invocations --compile --env dev     show what would run\n#\n#   A project with several sub-projects names as many as it likes:\n#   ./run-tests.sh <sub-project> <sub-project>\n#\n# An unknown sub-project name, or an environment this project does not declare, is an error\n# (exit 2) \u2014 never a silent no-op that runs nothing and reports success.\n#\n# WRITING THIS FILE FOR A PROJECT\n#   Three blocks below are marked \"EDIT FOR YOUR PROJECT\": the ENVS/SUBPROJECTS declarations,\n#   the `suite` table, and the optional setup/teardown hooks. Everything else is boilerplate \u2014\n#   copy it verbatim.\n#\n#   The `suite` table is the ONE place a project's config layering is written down: for each\n#   sub-project and each environment, the exact configs to layer, in merge order.\n#\nset -uo pipefail\n# `set -e` (exit on the first error) is not used to allow for more granular error handling.\n\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\"\n\n# Where this project sits relative to the compiler's mount root. Inside the DataSQRL agent the mount\n# root is the repository, so a project in a subdirectory is reached with the prefix the\n# orchestrator exports; empty everywhere else, meaning the project IS the mount root.\n#\n# It is passed as `-r <root>` rather than glued onto every config path. Both forms are equivalent\n# to the compiler, but `-r` is REQUIRED once `-b` points inside build/: without it the compiler\n# resolves script.main against the wrong root and fails with \"Could not find main SQRL script\".\nP=\"${SQRL_PACKAGE_PREFIX:-}\"\nif [ -n \"$P\" ]; then\n  ROOT=\"${P%/}\"                                   # the DataSQRL agent told us where we are\nelif ROOT=\"$(git rev-parse --show-prefix 2>/dev/null)\"; then\n  ROOT=\"${ROOT%/}\"; ROOT=\"${ROOT:-.}\"             # a repo checkout: our path within it\nelse\n  ROOT=\".\"                                        # not in a repo: this project is the root\nfi\n\n# The DataSQRL CLI version the DataSQRL agent container ships; CI and local runs default to the same\n# one so snapshots match. Override with SQRL_VERSION.\nSQRL_VERSION=\"${SQRL_VERSION:-0.12.5}\"\n# Fallback tag for when that version is not published yet (a release in flight). Resolved once,\n# on the first docker invocation, and never inside the DataSQRL agent \u2014 the container has its own CLI.\nSQRL_FALLBACK_IMAGE=\"${SQRL_FALLBACK_IMAGE:-datasqrl/cmd:dev}\"\nIMAGE=\"\"\n\nresolve_image() {\n  [ -n \"$IMAGE\" ] && return 0\n  local want=\"datasqrl/cmd:${SQRL_VERSION}\"\n  if docker image inspect \"$want\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || docker pull -q \"$want\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    IMAGE=\"$want\"\n    return 0\n  fi\n  IMAGE=\"$SQRL_FALLBACK_IMAGE\"\n  # Worth a warning, not a failure: snapshots were generated with the pinned version, so a\n  # different CLI can legitimately produce different output and fail tests that are fine.\n  printf 'warning: datasqrl/cmd:%s is not available; falling back to %s\\n' \\\n    \"$SQRL_VERSION\" \"$IMAGE\" >&2\n}\n\n# \u2500\u2500 EDIT FOR YOUR PROJECT \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n# The environments this project's configs cover, and the sub-projects it ships. Both are\n# declared rather than discovered, so that asking for something this project does not have\n# fails loudly instead of matching nothing, running zero suites and still exiting 0.\nENVS=\"test prod\"\nSUBPROJECTS=\"loan-payments loan-payments_table_test\"\n# \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nVERB=test\nENV=test\nLIST=\"\"\nSELECTED=\"\"\nwhile [ $# -gt 0 ]; do\n  case \"$1\" in\n    --compile)   VERB=compile ;;\n    --test)      VERB=test ;;\n    --env)       ENV=\"${2:-}\"; shift ;;\n    --env=*)     ENV=\"${1#--env=}\" ;;\n    --list-invocations) LIST=1 ;;\n    --list-envs) echo \"$ENVS\"; exit 0 ;;\n    --list-subprojects) echo \"$SUBPROJECTS\"; exit 0 ;;\n    -*)          echo \"unknown option: $1\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n    *)           SELECTED=\"$SELECTED $1\" ;;\n  esac\n  shift\ndone\ncase \" $ENVS \" in\n  *\" $ENV \"*) ;;\n  *) echo \"unknown env '$ENV' \u2014 this project declares: $ENVS\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\nesac\n\nfor s in $SELECTED; do\n  case \" $SUBPROJECTS \" in\n    *\" $s \"*) ;;\n    *) echo \"unknown sub-project '$s' \u2014 this project ships: $SUBPROJECTS\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n  esac\ndone\n\nselected() {\n  [ -z \"$SELECTED\" ] && return 0\n  case \" $SELECTED \" in *\" $1 \"*) return 0 ;; esac\n  return 1\n}\n\n# Each suite writes its own build folder (the -b flag in the driver loop below), so one suite's\n# artifacts never overwrite a sibling's. `-b <name>` names a subfolder of build/: DataSQRL\n# resolves `-b fraud_store` to <project-root>/build/fraud_store\n\nsqrl() {\n  local verb=\"$1\"; shift\n  # Every named config must exist. A missing one means the suite line and this environment\n  # disagree, and compiling a partial argument list would quietly review the wrong thing.\n  local a missing=0\n  for a in \"$@\"; do\n    case \"$a\" in\n      *.json) [ -f \"$a\" ] || { echo \"missing config: $a\" >&2; missing=1; } ;;\n    esac\n  done\n  [ \"$missing\" = 1 ] && return 1\n  # List mode: report what would run and return. Bash has already expanded the environment and\n  # the path prefix, so the caller reads the real argument list without parsing this file. The\n  # sub-project is named first so each line stands on its own.\n  if [ -n \"$LIST\" ]; then\n    printf 'SQRL_INVOCATION %s %s -r %s %s\\n' \"$SUITE\" \"$verb\" \"$ROOT\" \"$*\"\n    return 0\n  fi\n\n  if [ -x /opt/agent/cmd.sh ]; then\n    /opt/agent/cmd.sh \"$verb\" -r \"$ROOT\" \"$@\"     # inside the DataSQRL agent container\n    return\n  fi\n  # CI / local developer machine: run the DataSQRL CLI image. Mount the REPOSITORY root at\n  # /workspace (not just this project) so a sibling shared module this project consumes exists\n  # inside the container too; `-r <project>` then points the compiler at this project.\n  local root\n  root=\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null)\" || root=\"$PWD\"\n  # The image runs in UTC, and every template's snapshots are generated in UTC. The container's\n  # default is left alone. TZ passes through only when set explicitly.\n  resolve_image\n  docker run --rm ${TZ:+-e TZ=\"$TZ\"} -v \"$root\":/workspace \\\n    \"$IMAGE\" \"$verb\" -r \"$ROOT\" \"$@\"\n}\n\n# \u2500\u2500 EDIT FOR YOUR PROJECT (optional): setup \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n# Anything the suites need first \u2014 generating or downloading test data too large for git,\n# starting a fixture. Guard it with $LIST so listing stays instant and side-effect free.\n# [ -n \"$LIST\" ] || ./scripts/generate-testdata.sh || exit 1\n# \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n# \u2500\u2500 EDIT FOR YOUR PROJECT: the suite table \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n# One line per (sub-project, environment), naming that combination's configs in merge order \u2014\n# base first, environment config last, since a later file overrides an earlier one. Write the\n# filenames out literally; any names work. Cover every pair of SUBPROJECTS x ENVS that this\n# project actually has, and leave out the ones it does not: asking for a pair that is missing\n# reports an error rather than compiling something half-declared.\n#\n#   <sub-project>/<env>) echo \"<base config> <env config>\" ;;\n#\nsuite() {\n  case \"$1/$2\" in\n    loan-payments/test)             echo \"loan-payments-shared-package.json loan-payments-api-test-package.json\" ;;\n    loan-payments/prod)             echo \"loan-payments-shared-package.json loan-payments-prod-package.json\" ;;\n    loan-payments_table_test/test)  echo \"loan-payments-shared-package.json loan-payments-table-test-package.json\" ;;\n    *) return 1 ;;\n  esac\n}\n\n# \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n# Every selected sub-project runs even after one fails, so a single run reports every failure.\nfail=0\nSUITE=\"\"\nfor sub in $SUBPROJECTS; do\n  selected \"$sub\" || continue\n  SUITE=\"$sub\"\n  args=\"$(suite \"$sub\" \"$ENV\")\" || {\n    echo \"no '$ENV' configs declared for sub-project '$sub'\" >&2\n    fail=1\n    continue\n  }\n  # shellcheck disable=SC2086  # the declaration is a space-separated argument list, on purpose\n  sqrl \"$VERB\" $args -b \"$sub\" || fail=1\ndone\n\n# \u2500\u2500 EDIT FOR YOUR PROJECT (optional): teardown \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n# [ -n \"$LIST\" ] || ./scripts/teardown.sh\n# \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nexit $fail\n\n```\n\n\n## Output Format\n\nProvide your evaluation in the following JSON format:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"CRITICAL|HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW\",\n      \"description\": \"Description of the issue\",\n      \"location\": \"file name or path with extension\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n\n- List SQRL test coverage gaps with severity LOW. A sub-project suite the runner script never invokes is MEDIUM; runner setup or fail-accumulation gaps are LOW.\n- Your output must be valid JSON with the schema defined above."}
