using an upstream time-window or aggregating in the database if state can be large. (Location: Pipeline Definition) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] State table CustomerLoansSource has no valid event timestamp (Timestamp: -). (Location: Pipeline Definition) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] State table LoanPaymentSummarySource has no valid event timestamp (Timestamp: -). (Location: Pipeline Definition) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] State table LoanPaymentsSource has no valid event timestamp (Timestamp: -). (Location: Pipeline Definition) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] State table _AppliedPaymentAgg has no valid event timestamp (Timestamp: -). (Location: Pipeline Definition) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] State table _ReturnedPaymentAgg has no valid event timestamp (Timestamp: -). (Location: Pipeline Definition) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] CustomerLoansSource is a Flink state table with a stateful join between _LatestPersonalLoan and LoanPaymentSummarySource on loan_id; this may accumulate state over time. (Location: Pipeline Definition) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] LoanPaymentSummarySource is a Flink state table with stateful LEFT JOINs between _LatestPersonalLoan and the payment aggregation tables; this may accumulate state over time. (Location: Pipeline Definition) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] LoanPaymentsSource is a Flink state table with a stateful join between _LatestPersonalLoanPayment and _LatestPersonalLoan on loan_id; this may accumulate state over time. (Location: Pipeline Definition) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] _AppliedPaymentAgg is a Flink state table with a high-cardinality GROUP BY loan_id aggregation; this may accumulate state over time. (Location: Pipeline Definition) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] _ReturnedPaymentAgg is a Flink state table with a high-cardinality GROUP BY loan_id aggregation; this may accumulate state over time. (Location: Pipeline Definition) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [LOW] Stateful joins/aggregations in CustomerLoansSource, LoanPaymentSummarySource, LoanPaymentsSource, _AppliedPaymentAgg, and _ReturnedPaymentAgg could potentially be rewritten with time bounds (interval join, temporal join, or time-window aggregation) to reduce state accumulation, if the original requirements and semantics allow it. (Location: Pipeline Definition) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [LOW] Pipeline has no data quality (DQ_) or observability statistics (OB_) tables, nor tables with equivalent purpose by naming/definition/comments. (Location: Pipeline Definition) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [LOW] `CustomerLoansSource` has no test coverage, and its downstream `CustomerLoans` function also lacks tests. (Location: loan-payments.sqrl) (Verifier: tests)\n- [LOW] Parameterized functions `LoanPaymentSummary` and `LoanPayments` have no tests; their source tables are tested, but the function filters and parameter bindings are not covered. (Location: loan-payments.sqrl) (Verifier: tests)\n- [LOW] Source tables `Auto_Loan`, `Loan_Application`, and `Consumer_Loan_Delinquency_Event` are not used by any tested downstream table or function, so they have no coverage. (Location: loan-payments.sqrl) (Verifier: tests)\n- [LOW] The suite table omits `loan-payments_table_test/prod`, so running `./run-tests.sh --env prod` with no sub-project selection errors out instead of running all available prod suites. (Location: run-tests.sh) (Verifier: tests)\n- [MEDIUM] Internal tables LoanPaymentsSource, LoanPaymentSummarySource, and CustomerLoansSource do not start with an underscore and have no /** ... */ docstring. Even though they carry /*+no_query */, they are SQL-level tables consumers of the codebase will see, and they should be documented (or hidden with an underscore) so their purpose is clear. (Location: consumer_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: code)\n- [MEDIUM] Test tables with the /*+test */ hint lack a deterministic order: AutoLoanLeakTest, DuplicateLoanPaymentsTest, DuplicateLoanSummaryTest, ZeroPaymentSummaryTest. Add ORDER BY on the relevant key (or document explicitly if a single row is guaranteed) so test output is stable. (Location: consumer_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: code)\n- [LOW] LoanPaymentsSource, LoanPaymentSummarySource, and CustomerLoansSource are intermediate tables (marked /*+no_query */) but do not use the internal/hidden underscore prefix convention (e.g. _LoanPaymentsSource). Rename them to start with `_` so they are consistently treated as internal. (Location: consumer_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: code)\n- [LOW] There is insufficient documentation explaining why the intermediate hops (LoanPaymentsSource, LoanPaymentSummarySource, CustomerLoansSource) are declared with the /*+no_query */ hint, why the LEFT JOIN + COALESCE pattern is used in LoanPaymentSummarySource, and what each /*+test */ table verifies. Add -- comments so the intent is understandable without reverse-engineering the pipeline. (Location: consumer_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: code)\n- [HIGH] LoanPayments sink exposes customer_id derived from @pii primary_borrower_customer_id without @pii tag. (Location: LoanPayments) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [HIGH] LoanPayments sink exposes payment_amount_cents, principal_cents, interest_cents, and principal_balance_after_cents derived from @npi @confidential sources without @npi and @confidential tags. (Location: LoanPayments) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [HIGH] LoanPaymentSummary sink exposes customer_id derived from @pii primary_borrower_customer_id without @pii tag. (Location: LoanPaymentSummary) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [HIGH] LoanPaymentSummary sink exposes total_paid_cents, principal_paid_cents, and interest_paid_cents derived from @npi @confidential sources without @npi and @confidential tags; aggregation by loan_id does not declassify these tags. (Location: LoanPaymentSummary) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [HIGH] CustomerLoans sink exposes customer_id derived from @pii primary_borrower_customer_id without @pii tag. (Location: CustomerLoans) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [HIGH] CustomerLoans sink exposes original_amount_cents, current_balance_cents, monthly_payment_cents, total_paid_cents, principal_paid_cents, and interest_paid_cents derived from @npi @confidential sources without @npi and @confidential tags. (Location: CustomerLoans) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [HIGH] _AppliedPaymentAgg is a stateful, non-windowed GROUP BY aggregation in Flink that uses MAX(applied_date), a non-incremental aggregation function. On a retract stream this causes unbounded state growth because Flink must retain all prior records to correctly recompute the running maximum. Recommend an upstream time-window aggregation or delegating the MAX computation to the database if the state can grow large. (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] CustomerLoansSource is a `state` table in Flink with no valid event timestamp (Timestamp: -). Any table with Type in [state, stream, versioned_state] must expose a valid (event) timestamp. If time-windows were used, users would need to explicitly select and group by window_time. (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] LoanPaymentSummarySource is a `state` table in Flink with no valid event timestamp (Timestamp: -). (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] LoanPaymentsSource is a `state` table in Flink with no valid event timestamp (Timestamp: -). (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] _AppliedPaymentAgg is a `state` table in Flink with no valid event timestamp (Timestamp: -). (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] _ReturnedPaymentAgg is a `state` table in Flink with no valid event timestamp (Timestamp: -). (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] CustomerLoansSource is a `state` table computed in Flink and contains a stateful join (JOIN on loan_id between _LatestPersonalLoan and LoanPaymentSummarySource without any temporal or interval constraint). This may accumulate unbounded state over time. No mostRecentDistinct annotation is present. (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] LoanPaymentSummarySource is a `state` table computed in Flink and contains stateful LEFT JOINs on loan_id against _AppliedPaymentAgg and _ReturnedPaymentAgg without temporal or interval constraints. This may accumulate unbounded state over time. (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] LoanPaymentsSource is a `state` table computed in Flink and contains a stateful join (JOIN _LatestPersonalLoanPayment p JOIN _LatestPersonalLoan l ON p.loan_id = l.loan_id) with no temporal or interval constraint. This may accumulate unbounded state over time. (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] _AppliedPaymentAgg is a `state` table computed in Flink using a high-cardinality non-windowed GROUP BY on loan_id (~2e6 distinct keys), which may accumulate significant state over time. (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [MEDIUM] _ReturnedPaymentAgg is a `state` table computed in Flink using a high-cardinality non-windowed GROUP BY on loan_id (~2e6 distinct keys), which may accumulate significant state over time. (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [LOW] CustomerLoansSource's stateful join on loan_id between loan data and payment summary could be rewritten as a temporal join (FOR SYSTEM_TIME AS OF) if the semantics permit, avoiding unbounded state accumulation. This is a potential performance improvement only if the original requirements and semantics allow it. (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [LOW] LoanPaymentSummarySource's stateful LEFT JOINs against _AppliedPaymentAgg and _ReturnedPaymentAgg could be rewritten with time-bounds (interval/temporal joins) if semantics permit, avoiding state accumulation. Only applicable if requirements allow it. (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [LOW] LoanPaymentsSource's stateful join between payments and loans could be rewritten as a temporal join if the semantics permit, avoiding unbounded state accumulation. Only applicable if requirements allow it. (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [LOW] _AppliedPaymentAgg's non-windowed GROUP BY aggregation could be rewritten as a time-windowed aggregation (e.g. SESSION/TUMBLE over ingested_at) if the semantics permit, reducing state growth. Only applicable if requirements allow it. (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [LOW] _ReturnedPaymentAgg's non-windowed GROUP BY aggregation could be rewritten as a time-windowed aggregation if the semantics permit, reducing state growth. Only applicable if requirements allow it. (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [LOW] The pipeline contains no data-quality tables (DQ_ prefix or equivalent) and no observability/statistics tables (OB_ prefix or equivalent). Adding such tables would improve data quality monitoring and pipeline observability. (Location: cons_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: pipeline)\n- [LOW] CustomerLoansSource table definition has no test coverage and no downstream tables or functions that are tested; add a /*+test */ snapshot or no_rows test for CustomerLoansSource. (Location: consumer_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: tests)\n- [LOW] CustomerLoans API query (which filters CustomerLoansSource by customer_id) has no test coverage; no GraphQL test query or downstream consumer exercises it. (Location: consumer_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: tests)\n- [LOW] LoanPayments API query definition itself is untested; only its underlying LoanPaymentsSource is covered, so filter/order semantics of the query are not verified. (Location: consumer_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: tests)\n- [LOW] LoanPaymentSummary API query definition itself is untested; only its underlying LoanPaymentSummarySource is covered, so the loan_id/customer_id filter is not verified. (Location: consumer_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: tests)\n- [LOW] The source tables Auto_Loan, Loan_Application and Consumer_Loan_Delinquency_Event have no dedicated tests and no tested downstream consumers; the AutoLoanLeakTest only asserts absence of auto loans inside LoanPaymentsSource (which already filters loan_type='PERSONAL') and does not exercise Auto_Loan directly. (Location: consumer_loans.sqrl) (Verifier: tests)\n- [LOW] Runner performs no setup hook to generate or download the fixtures referenced by ${DATA_PATH} (consumer_loans-*.jsonl); the source connectors require these files, so a clean checkout cannot reproduce the test run. Add a guarded setup step (e.g. scripts/generate-testdata.sh under the $LIST guard). (Location: run-tests.sh) (Verifier: tests)\n\nFixing an issue means one of the following:\n1. Updating the implementation to implement a solution that fixes the issue. Use suggested solutions as a starting point.\n2. Adding documentation to the source code or README.md to explain why an identified issue does not apply, because:\n   1. You can deduce from the pipeline constraints or data semantics that the issue cannot arise (e.g. documenting that an aggregation `GROUP BY tenantId` does not result in unbounded state growth because we expect only 100s of tenants).\n   2. It's a known issue that won't be fixed (e.g. mark as `TODO` because it is not a priority right now or the risk is deemed low).\n\n**IMPORTANT**:\nOnly fix issues that are relevant to this implementation and compatible with the user requirements.\nUser requirements always take priority - do not implement fixes that contradict requirements. Add documentation when identified issues conflict with user requirements.\n\n**An issue on a file your plan did not ask you to touch is out of scope \u2014 leave it alone (option 3).**\nRewriting pre-existing, working code that you were not asked to change is unnecessary if it is not critical.\n\n**If you rename a table during refinement**\n- Update every reference to the old name across all `.sqrl` files (definitions, SELECT statements, test tables).\n- Invoke the `/test-sqrl` skill and run tests. Ensure tests pass.\n\n## Implementation\n\nMake sure to run tests and improve the codebase until tests pass. Run the project's test runner script, `./run-tests.sh`, scoped to the sub-projects your fixes touched: before running it, list every sub-project you edited plus every sub-project affected by an edit to shared code or configuration, and pass exactly those names as arguments. If a fix adds or renames a sub-project, add or update its suite line in `run-tests.sh`. For the details of the tests and the runner script, invoke the `/test-sqrl` skill.\n\nRead AGENTS.md for detailed DataSQRL syntax, patterns, and available tools!\n\n## Response\n\nWhen the fixes are done and the tests you ran pass, your final response must be ONLY the `./run-tests.sh` invocation you ran successfully, on one line, with the sub-project names you scoped it to (no arguments when you ran everything). No markdown, no explanation.\n\nCorrect response example:\n```\n./run-tests.sh [affected-sub-project-names] # only the affected sub-project(s) \n```\nand after a fix to shared code or configuration:\n```\n./run-tests.sh  # everything\n```"}], "timestamp": 1795511631558}}
