{"request_uuid": "a5a0a341-67dd-4fe9-88b6-c2c5702db363", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T09:15:13.486459+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "implementation", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "message_update", "usage": {"input": 364, "output": 1100, "cacheRead": 220928, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 684, "totalTokens": 222392, "cost": {"input": 0.0001092, "output": 0.00132, "cacheRead": 0.001325568, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.0027547680000000003}}, "assistantMessageEvent": {"type": "toolcall_end", "contentIndex": 2, "toolCall": {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20cd67b1f7193a7380e63", "name": "edit", "arguments": {"edits": [{"newText": "- **CDC dedup and no windows.** `DISTINCT ... ORDER BY source_updated_at DESC` keeps the latest\n  version per key, and the summary is an unwindowed, unbounded re-aggregation. A late or changed\n  payment updates the API within the freshness target (about one minute) instead of waiting for a\n  window boundary. The Flink state is bounded by key cardinality, not by time: the CDC dedup keeps\n  one state entry per loan and per payment, and the sources retain all payments, so state grows with\n  the number of loans and payments rather than with the stream length. Windows would contradict the\n  latest-status requirement, which is why none are used.", "oldText": "- **CDC dedup and no windows.** `DISTINCT ... ORDER BY source_updated_at DESC` keeps the latest\n  version per key, and the summary is an unwindowed, unbounded re-aggregation. A late or changed\n  payment updates the API within the freshness target (about one minute) instead of waiting for a\n  window boundary."}, {"newText": "| `ZeroPaymentSummaryTest` | a payment-free loan has zero counts/sums and a null last payment date |\n| `CustomerLoansSourceTest` | the four-loan customer `CUST-060` appears with one row per loan and its summary |", "oldText": "| `ZeroPaymentSummaryTest` | a payment-free loan has zero counts/sums and a null last payment date |"}], "path": "/workspace/loan-payments/README.md"}}}}
