{"request_uuid": "a5a0a341-67dd-4fe9-88b6-c2c5702db363", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T09:17:04.672634+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "implementation", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "message_start", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20cd82eb77b329539cf49", "toolName": "edit", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /workspace/loan-payments/README.md."}], "details": {"diff": "     ...\n  54   payment updates the API within the freshness target (about one minute) instead of waiting for a\n  55   window boundary. The Flink state is bounded by key cardinality, not by time: the CDC dedup keeps\n  56   one state entry per loan and per payment, and the sources retain all payments, so state grows with\n  57   the number of loans and payments rather than with the stream length. Windows would contradict the\n- 58   latest-status requirement, which is why none are used.\n+ 58   latest-status requirement, which is why none are used. For the same reason the summary and join\n+ 59   state tables carry no event timestamp: they are global state over the latest version per key, not\n+ 60   time-windowed streams, so there is no window to select a timestamp from.\n  59 - **Loans without payments.** `LoanPaymentSummarySource` is anchored on the latest personal loans\n  60   and left-joins the applied-payment aggregate, so `PL-011` and the other payment-free loans appear\n  61   with zero counts and sums and a null `last_payment_date`. Grouping only the payments would omit\n  62   them.\n     ...", "patch": "--- /workspace/loan-payments/README.md\n+++ /workspace/loan-payments/README.md\n@@ -54,9 +54,11 @@\n   payment updates the API within the freshness target (about one minute) instead of waiting for a\n   window boundary. The Flink state is bounded by key cardinality, not by time: the CDC dedup keeps\n   one state entry per loan and per payment, and the sources retain all payments, so state grows with\n   the number of loans and payments rather than with the stream length. Windows would contradict the\n-  latest-status requirement, which is why none are used.\n+  latest-status requirement, which is why none are used. For the same reason the summary and join\n+  state tables carry no event timestamp: they are global state over the latest version per key, not\n+  time-windowed streams, so there is no window to select a timestamp from.\n - **Loans without payments.** `LoanPaymentSummarySource` is anchored on the latest personal loans\n   and left-joins the applied-payment aggregate, so `PL-011` and the other payment-free loans appear\n   with zero counts and sums and a null `last_payment_date`. Grouping only the payments would omit\n   them.\n", "firstChangedLine": 58}, "isError": false, "durationMs": 9, "timestamp": 1795511824671}}
