e API documentation carries the same classification."}, {"newText": "-- FR-7: only APPLIED payments contribute to the totals and the last payment date. Aggregating in\n-- Flink keeps the summary fresh without a window boundary. MAX(applied_date) is non-incremental,\n-- but the per-loan state it keeps is bounded by the number of applied payments of that loan (the\n-- dataset is finite: the sources retain all payments and the dedup keeps one version per key).\n-- Alternatives are rejected on purpose: a time window would break the latest-status/no-window\n-- requirement, and aggregating in the database would recompute on every request instead of serving\n-- the pre-aggregated, always-current summary.", "oldText": "-- FR-7: only APPLIED payments contribute to the totals and the last payment date. Aggregating in\n-- Flink keeps the summary fresh without a window boundary (state is bounded by loan cardinality,\n-- one state entry per loan key; the sources retain all payments and the dedup keeps one per key)."}], "path": "/workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments.sqrl"}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "together", "model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash", "usage": {"input": 546, "output": 1377, "cacheRead": 226816, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 857, "totalTokens": 228739, "cost": {"input": 0.0001638, "output": 0.0016523999999999998, "cacheRead": 0.001360896, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.003177096}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1795511831186, "responseId": "948c8b64b3fe4795b88ed09487094d03-aws_ec1", "rawStopReason": "tool_calls", "durationMs": 4987, "thinkingLevel": "high"}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20cd85a137d70b9456556", "toolName": "edit", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced 2 block(s) in /workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments.sqrl."}], "details": {"diff": "     ...\n  30 --\n  31 -- Kept hidden (`_`) and queried only through the public `LoanPayments` function, which adds the\n  32 -- customer_id claim filter. The `@pii`/`@npi`/`@confidential` tags below propagate from the catalog\n  33 -- columns so the API documentation carries the same classification.\n+ 34 --\n+ 35 -- State note: this is a regular join, but both sides are deduplicated versioned-state tables with\n+ 36 -- at most one row per key, so Flink keeps one entry per loan_id, not one per event. The join state\n+ 37 -- is therefore bounded by the number of loans and payments, not by the length of the streams.\n  34 /** Internal: personal-loan payments enriched with the customer and purpose of their loan.\n  35 # Columns:\n  36 - payment_id: Unique identifier of the payment.\n  37 - loan_id: The loan the payment belongs to.\n     ...\n  76   FROM _LatestPersonalLoanPayment p\n  77   JOIN _LatestPersonalLoan l ON p.loan_id = l.loan_id;\n  78 \n  79 -- FR-7: only APPLIED payments contribute to the totals and the last payment date. Aggregating in\n- 80 -- Flink keeps the summary fresh without a window boundary (state is bounded by loan cardinality,\n- 81 -- one state entry per loan key; the sources retain all payments and the dedup keeps one per key).\n+ 84 -- Flink keeps the summary fresh without a window boundary. MAX(applied_date) is non-incremental,\n+ 85 -- but the per-loan state it keeps is bounded by the number of applied payments of that loan (the\n+ 86 -- dataset is finite: the sources retain all payments and the dedup keeps one version per key).\n+ 87 -- Alternatives are rejected on purpose: a time window would break the latest-status/no-window\n+ 88 -- requirement, and aggregating in the database would recompute on every request instead of serving\n+ 89 -- the pre-aggregated, always-current summary.\n  82 _AppliedPaymentAgg :=\n  83   SELECT loan_id,\n  84          COUNT(*) AS applied_payment_count,\n  85          SUM(payment_amount_cents) AS total_paid_cents,\n     ...", "patch": "--- /workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments.sqrl\n+++ /workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments.sqrl\n@@ -30,8 +30,12 @@\n --\n -- Kept hidden (`_`) and queried only through the public `LoanPayments` function, which adds the\n -- customer_id claim filter. The `@pii`/`@npi`/`@confidential` tags below propagate from the catalog\n -- columns so the API documentation carries the same classification.\n+--\n+-- State note: this is a regular join, but both sides are deduplicated versioned-state tables with\n+-- at most one row per key, so Flink keeps one entry per loan_id, not one per event. The join state\n+-- is therefore bounded by the number of loans and payments, not by the length of the streams.\n /** Internal: personal-loan payments enriched with the customer and purpose of their loan.\n # Columns:\n - payment_id: Unique identifier of the payment.\n - loan_id: The loan the payment belongs to.\n@@ -76,10 +80,14 @@\n   FROM _LatestPersonalLoanPayment p\n   JOIN _LatestPersonalLoan l ON p.loan_id = l.loan_id;\n \n -- FR-7: only APPLIED payments contribute to the totals and the last payment date. Aggregating in\n--- Flink keeps the summary fresh without a window boundary (state is bounded by loan cardinality,\n--- one state entry per loan key; the sources retain all payments and the dedup keeps one per key).\n+-- Flink keeps the summary fresh without a window boundary. MAX(applied_date) is non-incremental,\n+-- but the per-loan state it keeps is bounded by the number of applied payments of that loan (the\n+-- dataset is finite: the sources retain all payments and the dedup keeps one version per key).\n+-- Alternatives are rejected on purpose: a time window would break the latest-status/no-window\n+-- requirement, and aggregating in the database would recompute on every request instead of serving\n+-- the pre-aggregated, always-current summary.\n _AppliedPaymentAgg :=\n   SELECT loan_id,\n          COUNT(*) AS applied_payment_count,\n          SUM(payment_amount_cents) AS total_paid_cents,\n", "firstChangedLine": 34}, "isError": false, "durationMs": 4, "timestamp": 1795511836179}, {"role": "ass