{"request_uuid": "a5a0a341-67dd-4fe9-88b6-c2c5702db363", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T09:24:50.300732+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "implementation", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "message_start", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20cdf48187401b5c80cdb", "toolName": "edit", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced 2 block(s) in /workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments.sqrl."}], "details": {"diff": "     ...\n 114   GROUP BY loan_id;\n 115 \n 116 -- FR-6: one row per personal loan. Anchored on the latest loans and LEFT JOINed to both aggregates,\n 117 -- so a loan without payments still appears; COALESCE turns its missing counts and sums into 0 and\n-118 -- leaves last_payment_date null. Grouping only the payments would omit those loans.\n+118 -- leaves last_payment_date null. Grouping only the payments would omit those loans. Returned\n+119 -- payments are a separate LEFT JOIN because they count toward returned_payment_count but must not\n+120 -- contribute to any amount. Both sides are deduplicated keyed tables, so each join keeps one entry\n+121 -- per loan_id, and the state is bounded by the number of loans rather than the stream length.\n 119 /** Internal: per-loan payment counts, totals and last applied payment date for every personal loan.\n 120 # Columns:\n 121 - loan_id: The loan this summary describes.\n 122 - customer_id: The primary borrower of the loan. @pii\n     ...\n 144   LEFT JOIN _AppliedPaymentAgg a ON l.loan_id = a.loan_id\n 145   LEFT JOIN _ReturnedPaymentAgg r ON l.loan_id = r.loan_id;\n 146 \n 147 -- FR-11: the signed-in customer's loans with their summary and the loan details the client shows.\n+151 -- The summary is already derived from _LatestPersonalLoan, but this join is what adds the loan\n+152 -- detail columns (status, balances, next due date) to it; it is a one-row-per-loan lookup, not a\n+153 -- re-aggregation, so it keeps one state entry per loan_id.\n 148 -- This is a hidden internal table; the public `CustomerLoans` function adds the claim filter.\n 149 /** Internal: every personal loan with its summary and the loan details the client displays.\n 150 # Columns:\n 151 - loan_id: The loan identifier.\n     ...", "patch": "--- /workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments.sqrl\n+++ /workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments.sqrl\n@@ -114,9 +114,12 @@\n   GROUP BY loan_id;\n \n -- FR-6: one row per personal loan. Anchored on the latest loans and LEFT JOINed to both aggregates,\n -- so a loan without payments still appears; COALESCE turns its missing counts and sums into 0 and\n--- leaves last_payment_date null. Grouping only the payments would omit those loans.\n+-- leaves last_payment_date null. Grouping only the payments would omit those loans. Returned\n+-- payments are a separate LEFT JOIN because they count toward returned_payment_count but must not\n+-- contribute to any amount. Both sides are deduplicated keyed tables, so each join keeps one entry\n+-- per loan_id, and the state is bounded by the number of loans rather than the stream length.\n /** Internal: per-loan payment counts, totals and last applied payment date for every personal loan.\n # Columns:\n - loan_id: The loan this summary describes.\n - customer_id: The primary borrower of the loan. @pii\n@@ -144,8 +147,11 @@\n   LEFT JOIN _AppliedPaymentAgg a ON l.loan_id = a.loan_id\n   LEFT JOIN _ReturnedPaymentAgg r ON l.loan_id = r.loan_id;\n \n -- FR-11: the signed-in customer's loans with their summary and the loan details the client shows.\n+-- The summary is already derived from _LatestPersonalLoan, but this join is what adds the loan\n+-- detail columns (status, balances, next due date) to it; it is a one-row-per-loan lookup, not a\n+-- re-aggregation, so it keeps one state entry per loan_id.\n -- This is a hidden internal table; the public `CustomerLoans` function adds the claim filter.\n /** Internal: every personal loan with its summary and the loan details the client displays.\n # Columns:\n - loan_id: The loan identifier.\n", "firstChangedLine": 118}, "isError": false, "durationMs": 7, "timestamp": 1795512290300}}
