{"request_uuid": "a5a0a341-67dd-4fe9-88b6-c2c5702db363", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T09:25:00.331809+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "implementation", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "turn_end", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "The dedup tables retain `ingested_at TIMESTAMP_LTZ(3) *ROWTIME*`. The join's result has no timestamp. DataSQRL likely assigns the timestamp based on the rowtime marker. If I write `GREATEST(p.ingested_at, l.ingested_at) AS ...`, the result column may lose the `*ROWTIME*` marker.\n\nLet me try an experiment. I'll add to `_LoanPaymentsSource`:\n```\n         GREATEST(p.ingested_at, l.ingested_at) AS _rowtime\n```\nand compile. If timestamp becomes `_rowtime`, good.\n\nBut `GREATEST` returns TIMESTAMP_LTZ(3)? Both are TIMESTAMP_LTZ(3). It should.\n\nHowever, there's a subtlety: `_LoanPaymentsSource` uses `SELECT p.column` explicitly, not `SELECT *`. The `ingested_at` columns are available. Let me add.\n\nLet me do the experiment with a temporary edit, compile, and check. If it works, apply to `_LoanPaymentSummarySource` and `_CustomerLoansSource`.\n\nFor `_LoanPaymentSummarySource`: join `_LatestPersonalLoan l LEFT JOIN _AppliedPaymentAgg a LEFT JOIN _ReturnedPaymentAgg r`. The aggregates don't have timestamps. If I add `MAX(ingested_at)` to the aggregates, then GREATEST across. But the aggregates over a watermark column... Let me first test the join.\n\nActually, for a left join, the skill says: \"In an outer join, wrap the timestamp of each side that can be missing in COALESCE with the timestamp of another side. For example, in a LEFT JOIN, write GREATEST(l.ts, COALESCE(r.ts, l.ts)).\" So for `_LoanPaymentSummarySource`: `GREATEST(l.ingested_at, COALESCE(a.ingested_at, l.ingested_at), COALESCE(r.ingested_at, l.ingested_at))`.\n\nBut the aggregates need an `ingested_at` timestamp. I could add `MAX(ingested_at) AS ingested_at` to the aggregates. But MAX over the rowtime. Hmm.\n\nThis is getting complicated and risky. Given the verifier only needs \"a valid event timestamp\", maybe adding the `GREATEST` column will make the compiler assign the timestamp. Let me test with a single edit and compile.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the risk/benefit. The state timestamp issues are MEDIUM. Adding timestamps could change the pipeline semantics and break snapshots (new hidden column, maybe different ordering). It could also introduce the \"not monotonically increasing\" issues. Given the requirements don't need the timestamp and the tables are end-state state tables served via Postgres, the timestamp is not needed. Documentation is the safer, requirement-compatible choice.\n\nBut the verifier has flagged it three times. The task says \"Add documentation when identified issues conflict with user requirements.\" The requirements mandate an unwindowed summary. A state table without a timestamp is a consequence. I'll document clearly in the README and code.\n\nHowever, for the joins, we could add the timestamp without changing semantics. Let me at least try the `_LoanPaymentsSource` experiment. If it works cleanly, it addresses 2 of the 5 tables (the joins). The aggregates and summary would remain.\n\nActually, let me test quickly. Let me make a temporary edit adding `GREATEST(p.ingested_at, l.ingested_at) AS _event_time` and compile. Let me not commit if it doesn't work.\n\nHmm, but I'm worried about wasting a compile cycle. Compiles are ~3s. Fine.\n\nLet me do it.\n\nWait, but the public function `LoanPayments` does `SELECT *` from `_LoanPaymentsSource`; adding a hidden `_event_time` column won't be exposed. Good.\n\nLet me add and compile.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Let me experiment with adding an event timestamp to the join table to see if DataSQRL picks it up."}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20cdf619b7e339074af35", "name": "edit", "arguments": {"edits": [{"newText": "         p.confirmation_number,\n         p.return_reason_code,\n         GREATEST(p.ingested_at, l.ingested_at) AS _event_time", "oldText": "         p.confirmation_number,\n         p.return_reason_code"}], "path": "/workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments.sqrl"}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20cdf62137af089ed4329", "name": "bash", "arguments": {"command": "cd /workspace/loan-payments && /opt/agent/cmd.sh compile -r loan-payments loan-payments-shared-package.json loan-payments-api-test-package.json -b loan-payments > /tmp/loanpay_c3.log 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\"; grep -iE \"error|BUILD\" /tmp/loanpay_c3.log | tail -5; python3 -c \"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('build/loan-payments/pipeline_explain.json'))\nfor t in d:\n    if t.get('name') in ('_LoanPaymentsSource',):\n        print(t['name'],'timestamp=',t.get('timestamp'))\n        for c in t.get('schema',[]):\n            if 'time' in c['name'].lower(): print('  ',c['name'],c['type'])\n\"", "timeout": 600}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "together", "model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash", "usage": {"input": 930, "output": 1212, "cacheRead": 247168, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 835, "totalTokens": 249310, "cost": {"input": 0.000279, "output": 0.0014544, "cacheRead": 0.001483008, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.003216408}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1795512291795, "responseId": "07e05e0fa9904638a83e48564b63bf1d-aws_ec1", "rawStopReason": "tool_calls", "durationMs": 4437, "thinkingLevel": "high"}, "toolResults": [{"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20cdf619b7e339074af35", "toolName": "edit", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments.sqrl."}], "details": {"diff": "     ...\n  81          p.payment_method,\n  82          p.principal_balance_after_cents,\n  83          p.days_past_due_at_payment,\n  84          p.confirmation_number,\n- 85          p.return_reason_code\n+ 85          p.return_reason_code,\n+ 86     