date). Adding another MAX doesn't worsen. Actually, it might. But the timestamp is metadata.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can avoid aggregates entirely by using the `_event_time` from the source and let DataSQRL infer. Let me test whether `_AppliedPaymentAgg` gets a timestamp automatically now that its input has one. Let me check current pipeline_explain (after the compile). Let me print timestamps for all our tables.\n\nActually, let me just check. If aggregates still have \"-\", I'll try adding MAX.\n\nLet me check timestamps now."}
