{"request_uuid": "a5a0a341-67dd-4fe9-88b6-c2c5702db363", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T09:25:07.828845+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "implementation", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "message_update", "usage": {"input": 169, "output": 1195, "cacheRead": 250112, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 608, "totalTokens": 251476, "cost": {"input": 5.07e-05, "output": 0.001434, "cacheRead": 0.001500672, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.002985372}}, "assistantMessageEvent": {"type": "thinking_end", "contentIndex": 0, "content": "Aggregates still \"-\". Let me add `MAX(_event_time) AS _event_time` to the aggregates and the GREATEST to the summary/customer joins.\n\nFor `_AppliedPaymentAgg`:\n```\nSELECT loan_id,\n       COUNT(*) AS applied_payment_count,\n       ...\n       MAX(applied_date) AS last_payment_date,\n       MAX(_event_time) AS _event_time\nFROM _LoanPaymentsSource\nWHERE payment_status='APPLIED'\nGROUP BY loan_id;\n```\n\nFor `_ReturnedPaymentAgg`:\n```\nSELECT loan_id, COUNT(*) AS returned_payment_count,\n       MAX(_event_time) AS _event_time\nFROM _LoanPaymentsSource\nWHERE payment_status='RETURNED'\nGROUP BY loan_id;\n```\n\nFor `_LoanPaymentSummarySource`:\n```\nSELECT l.loan_id, ..., a.last_payment_date,\n       GREATEST(l._event_time, COALESCE(a._event_time, l._event_time), COALESCE(r._event_time, l._event_time)) AS _event_time\nFROM _LatestPersonalLoan l\nLEFT JOIN _AppliedPaymentAgg a ...\nLEFT JOIN _ReturnedPaymentAgg r ...\n```\n\nFor `_CustomerLoansSource`:\n```\nSELECT l.loan_id, ..., s.last_payment_date,\n       GREATEST(l._event_time, s._event_time) AS _event_time\nFROM _LatestPersonalLoan l\nJOIN _LoanPaymentSummarySource s ...\n```\n\nWait, `_LatestPersonalLoan` has `ingested_at` (rowtime) but not `_event_time`. In `_LoanPaymentSummarySource`, I used `l._event_time` but `_LatestPersonalLoan` has `ingested_at`. Let me use `l.ingested_at`. And in `_CustomerLoansSource`, the join is `_LatestPersonalLoan l JOIN _LoanPaymentSummarySource s`, so `GREATEST(l.ingested_at, s._event_time)`.\n\nLet me be careful:\n- `_AppliedPaymentAgg._event_time` = MAX(source `_event_time`)\n- `_ReturnedPaymentAgg._event_time` = MAX(source `_event_time`)\n- `_LoanPaymentSummarySource`: `GREATEST(l.ingested_at, COALESCE(a._event_time, l.ingested_at), COALESCE(r._event_time, l.ingested_at))`\n- `_CustomerLoansSource`: `GREATEST(l.ingested_at, s._event_time)`\n\nLet me apply these edits and compile. If the aggregates' timestamps become `_event_time`, great.\n\nBut wait: does DataSQRL recognize `MAX(_event_time) AS _event_time` as the rowtime? The `_event_time` column in `_LoanPaymentsSource` is marked `*ROWTIME*`. `MAX` of it might lose the marker. Let me test.\n\nLet me apply."}}
