ue: The verifier claims the filesystem source re-lists and double-counts. Adding a timestamp doesn't fix that. But it's test-only. For prod, Kafka. Document.\n\nNow let me also reconsider: are the `_event_time` columns going to appear in the Postgres sink tables? They're hidden, so likely not. Let me verify the postgres.json doesn't include `_event_time`. Actually, it might include hidden columns in the physical table but not the API. Let me check. If it creates a column `_event_time` in Postgres, that's fine.\n\nNow let me run the tests. Also, I should verify the API snapshots are unchanged.\n\nBefore running, let me double-check the `run-tests.sh` syntax with the new `if` block. Let me run `--list-invocations` first (fast, no side effects; the setup guard is skipped for LIST).\n\nThen run the full test.\n\nLet me also update the README to mention the event timestamp? The README currently says state tables carry no event timestamp. That's now false! I need to update that sentence. Let me fix:\n\nCurrent README:\n\"...For the same reason the summary and join state tables carry no event timestamp: they are global state over the latest version per key, not time-windowed streams, so there is no window to select a timestamp from.\"\n\nNow they DO carry `_event_time`. Let me update: \"The state tables carry a derived event timestamp `_event_time` (the greatest `ingested_at` of the rows that produced the state), computed from the source event time rather than a window.\"\n\nLet me update README.\n\nAlso, I should update the code comments to mention the timestamp. Not strictly necessary.\n\nLet me update README.\n\nThen run tests.\n\nLet me also verify the `--env prod` list still works with the new setup block. The setup block checks `$LIST`; in list mode it's skipped. Good.\n\nLet me update README.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "text", "text": "All state tables now have a valid `_event_time` timestamp. Let me update the README statement that said otherwise."}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20cdfb870798383033c32", "name": "edit", "arguments": {"edits": [{"newText": "  the number of loans and payments rather than with the stream length. Windows would contradict the\n  latest-status requirement, which is why none are used. The state tables instead carry a derived\n  event timestamp `_event_time` (the greatest `ingested_at` of the rows that produced the state), so\n  they keep valid event-time semantics without a window.", "oldText": "  the number of loans and payments rather than with the stream length. Windows would contradict the\n  latest-status requirement, which is why none are used. For the same reason the summary and join\n  state tables carry no event timestamp: they are global state over the latest version per key, not\n  time-windowed streams, so there is no window to select a timestamp from."}], "path": "/workspace/loan-payments/README.md"}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "together", "model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash", "usage": {"input": 247, "output": 1071, "cacheRead": 251648, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 817, "totalTokens": 252966, "cost": {"input": 7.41e-05, "output": 0.0012852, "cacheRead": 0.001509888, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.002869188}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1795512314353, "responseId": "a68fe09f15c04cc99acdc3c9048be24a-aws_ec1", "rawStopReason": "tool_calls", "durationMs": 3995, "thinkingLevel": "high"}, "toolResults": [{"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_01a20cdfb870798383033c32", "toolName": "edit", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /workspace/loan-payments/README.md."}], "details": {"diff": "     ...\n  54   payment updates the API within the freshness target (about one minute) instead of waiting for a\n  55   window boundary. The Flink state is bounded by key cardinality, not by time: the CDC dedup keeps\n  56   one state entry per loan and per payment, and the sources retain all payments, so state grows with\n  57   the number of loans and payments rather than with the stream length. Windows would contradict the\n- 58   latest-status requirement, which is why none are used. For the same reason the summary and join\n- 59   state tables carry no event timestamp: they are global state over the latest version per key, not\n- 60   time-windowed streams, so there is no window to select a timestamp from.\n+ 58   latest-status requirement, which is why none are used. The state tables instead carry a derived\n+ 59   event timestamp `_event_time` (the greatest `ingested_at` of the rows that produced the state), so\n+ 60   they keep valid event-time semantics without a window.\n  61 - **Loans without payments.** `LoanPaymentSummarySource` is anchored on the latest personal loans\n  62   and left-joins the applied-payment aggregate, so `PL-011` and the other payment-free loans appear\n  63   with zero counts and sums and a null `last_payment_date`. Grouping only the payments would omit\n  64   them.\n     ...", "patch": "--- /workspace/loan-payments/README.md\n+++ /workspace/loan-payments/README.md\n@@ -54,11 +54,11 @@\n   payment updates the API within the freshness target (about one minute) instead of waiting for a\n   window boundary. The Flink state is bounded by key cardinality, not by time: the CDC dedup keeps\n   one state entry per loan and per payment, and the sources retain all payments, so state grows with\n   the number of loans and payments rather than with the stream length. Windows would contradict the\n-  latest-status requirement, which is why none are used. For the same reason the summary and join\n-  state tables carry no event timestamp: they are global state over the latest version per key, not\n-  time-windowed streams, so there is no window to select a timestamp from.\n+  latest-status requirement, which is why none are used. The state tables instead carry a derived\n+  event timestamp `_event_time` (the greatest `ingested_at` of the rows that produced the state), so\n+  they keep valid event-time semantics without a window.\n - **Loans without payments.** `LoanPaymentSummarySource` is anchored on the latest personal loans\n   and left-joins the applied-payment aggregate, so `PL-011` and the other payment-free loans appear\n   with zero counts and sums and a null `last_payment_date`. Grouping only the payments would omit\n   them.\n", "firstChangedLine": 58}, "isError": false, "durationMs": 5, "timestamp": 1795512318355}]}
