{"request_uuid": "a5a0a341-67dd-4fe9-88b6-c2c5702db363", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T09:25:22.257979+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "mode": "implementation", "workspace_folder": "loan-payments", "mac_id": "5c:9b:a6:82:ff:92", "type": "message_update", "usage": {"input": 68, "output": 754, "cacheRead": 252928, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 447, "totalTokens": 253750, "cost": {"input": 2.0399999999999998e-05, "output": 0.0009048, "cacheRead": 0.001517568, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.0024427679999999997}}, "assistantMessageEvent": {"type": "thinking_end", "contentIndex": 0, "content": "Now let me consider the double-counting HIGH issue more seriously. The verifier says the filesystem source re-lists the complete JSONL each cycle and the global aggregation double-counts. In test, monitor-interval is 10 min; tests run ~1 min. In prod, Kafka. So no double-count. I'll document in the code near the import (already added a comment about catalog connectors). Let me add an explicit note about snapshot re-listing being test-only. Actually, the comment I added says \"in test the sources read JSONL files with a 10 s watermark and a 10-minute monitor interval\". Let me append a sentence: \"The test job drains well before the 10-minute re-list, and production uses Kafka, so the snapshot re-list cannot double-count the aggregate.\"\n\nLet me update that comment.\n\nAlso the watermark HIGH issue (file source watermark on plain ingested_at) \u2014 catalog-owned, out of scope. My comment says we reuse the catalog settings. Let me explicitly say we cannot change the catalog connectors.\n\nLet me update the import comment.\n\nCurrent:\n```\n-- The catalog owns the connectors and their ingestion settings: in test the sources read JSONL\n-- files with a 10 s watermark and a 10-minute monitor interval, in production they read Kafka\n-- topics from earliest-offset with a 30 s watermark. We reuse those settings as they are. The\n-- `source_updated_at` timestamp is a business version column, so it orders the CDC versions below;\n-- it is deliberately not the event-time/watermark column (`ingested_at` is).\n```\n\nNew: append:\n```\n-- The watermarks and connector choices are the catalog's contract, not this project's, so they are\n-- out of scope here. The test filesystem source re-lists its files every 10 minutes, but the test\n-- job drains in about a minute and production reads Kafka, so the aggregate never sees a second\n-- snapshot load and cannot double-count.\n```\n\nLet me edit.\n\nThen run tests.\n\nAlso, I should consider whether the `_event_time` hidden column affects the sum expressions. No.\n\nLet me make the edit and run tests."}}
