 filesystem source re-lists its files every 10 minutes, but the test\n-- job drains in about a minute and production reads Kafka, so the aggregate never sees a second\n-- snapshot load and cannot double-count.\n```\n\nLet me edit.\n\nThen run tests.\n\nAlso, I should consider whether the `_event_time` hidden column affects the sum expressions. No.\n\nLet me make the edit and run tests.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20cdfc71d702095c8d935", "name": "edit", "arguments": {"edits": [{"newText": "-- `source_updated_at` timestamp is a business version column, so it orders the CDC versions below;\n-- it is deliberately not the event-time/watermark column (`ingested_at` is). The watermarks and\n-- connector choices are the catalog's contract, not this project's, so they are out of scope here.\n-- The test filesystem source re-lists its files every 10 minutes, but the test job drains in about\n-- a minute and production reads Kafka, so the aggregates never see a second snapshot load and\n-- cannot double-count rows.", "oldText": "-- `source_updated_at` timestamp is a business version column, so it orders the CDC versions below;\n-- it is deliberately not the event-time/watermark column (`ingested_at` is)."}], "path": "/workspace/loan-payments/loan-payments.sqrl"}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20cdfc8507610811234ab", "name": "bash", "arguments": {"command": "cd /workspace/loan-payments && SQRL_PACKAGE_PREFIX=loan-payments/ ./run-tests.sh --list-invocations --env prod; echo \"list_exit=$?\""}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "together", "model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash", "usage": {"input": 68, "output": 754, "cacheRead": 252928, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 447, "totalTokens": 253750, "cost": {"input": 2.0399999999999998e-05, "output": 0.0009048, "cacheRead": 0.001517568, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.0024427679999999997}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1795512318358, "responseId": "9b7a3733f8