omment) and README. The script comment change came after the last test? Let me check: I ran the test (`loanpay_final3`) after adding `_event_time` and the comment edits? Sequence:\n1. Added `_event_time` to join, compiled.\n2. Added `_event_time` to aggregates + summary + customer, compiled.\n3. Updated README.\n4. Added import comment about double-counting (edit), then ran `--list-invocations`.\n5. Ran full test `loanpay_final3` \u2192 passed.\n6. Then README edits.\n\nSo the script's last change (import comment) was before `loanpay_final3`. Good. Since then only README. So tests are valid. But the task requires the final action to be a successful run-tests.sh. Let me run it once more to be safe.\n\nActually, wait\u2014did I make any script changes after `loanpay_final3`? Let me check: After `loanpay_final3`, I only edited README (twice). So no. But to comply, I'll run the final test again.\n\nLet me run the full test. Since both sub-projects are affected (shared code), no args is appropriate (runs everything). Actually the instruction says pass the sub-projects touched. Both touched \u2192 no args (everything). Let me run `./run-tests.sh`.\n\nLet me do the final run.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "text", "text": "All fixes are in. Let me do the final full test run."}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_01a20ce139e570c1b47e01f9", "name": "bash", "arguments": {"command": "cd /workspace/loan-payments && SQRL_PACKAGE_PREFIX=loan-payments/ ./run-tests.sh > /tmp/loanpay_final4.log 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\"; grep -E \"Tests run|BUILD SUCCESS|BUILD FAILURE|COMPILE_DONE\" /tmp/loanpay_final4.log", "timeout": 900}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "together", "model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash", "usage": {"input": 41, "output": 503, "cacheRead": 257792, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 358, "totalTokens": 258336, "cost": {"input": 1.2299999999999999e-05, "output": 0.0006035999999999999, "cacheRead": 0.001546752, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.0